e tendon warm through.", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:25 – 9:45/mi, HR under 150", "distanceM": 11265, "structure": "7 mi steady easy"}, "date": "2026-09-30", "notes": "Midweek aerobic. Keep this in Z2 — it drifted to Z3 last week.", "dayType": "easy", "strength": "Short strength: hips, core, slow heel drops."}, {"run": {"type": "quality", "shoes": "Saucony Endorphin Speed 4", "paceOrHr": "MP 8:00/mi, recoveries 9:45/mi", "distanceM": 12070, "structure": "2 mi WU · 2 x 2 mi at 8:00/mi w/ 3 min easy jog · 1 mi CD"}, "date": "2026-10-01", "notes": "Longer MP touch than last week, still short of September's tempo. Flat canal only — no hills.", "dayType": "quality"}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "notes": "Fixed rest, travel. Walk, eat, sleep well for Sunday.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:30 – 9:50/mi", "distanceM": 6437, "structure": "4 mi easy"}, "date": "2026-10-03", "notes": "Short easy hour on legs to set up Sunday. Properly easy.", "dayType": "easy", "strength": "Second strength session: heel drops, hips, core."}, {"run": {"type": "long", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "First 12 mi 9:30 – 9:50/mi, last 2 mi 8:00 – 8:05/mi", "distanceM": 22531, "structure": "12 mi steady easy, then 2 mi at MP 8:00 – 8:05/mi"}, "date": "2026-10-04", "notes": "14 mi with a short MP finish — first MP-on-tired-legs since the Achilles. Drop the MP if anything whispers in the first 10.", "dayType": "long"}], "week": "2026-W40"}}, {"isoWeek": "2026-W39", "analysis": "## Where we are\\n\\nYou lost about a week of load but the aerobic base is intact. Easy pace is still 9:20 – 9:30/mi at HR 142 – 143, and the Sunday long run drifted a reasonable +8 bpm over 8 miles. That is a healthy platform to build from with eight weeks until Lakeshore.\\n\\n## Why this shape\\n\\nThe physio cleared one short tempo, so Thursday is deliberately small: a 2-mile tempo at 8:15 – 8:25/mi, not marathon pace. Short enough to test the Achilles under load, long enough to feel like a workout. If morning stiffness returns at any point before Thursday, swap it for an easy 5.\\n\\nThe long run moves back to 12 miles at pure easy effort. No marathon pace finish this week — we need two clean weeks of tempo and long run before layering goal pace on tired legs again. If Sunday goes well, the week of Sep 28 goes to 14 and we start reintroducing MP work the week after.\\n\\n## Easy running\\n\\nThree of the four easy runs last week crept toward 9:17 – 9:20/mi. That is sharper than it needs to be in a rebuild week. Open every run at 10:00/mi for the first mile and let HR, not pace, decide the rest.\\n\\n## Keep doing\\n\\nTwice-daily heel drops, the two short strength sessions, and the pre-run stiffness check. If first-mile stiffness ever rises above a 3/10 or sharpens with pace, stop the run and tell me — that is the signal the physio gave you, and it is the right one.", "recapMarkdown": "# Weekly Recap — 2026-W39 (Mon Sep 21 – Sun Sep 27, 2026)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Mileage | 34.83 mi | 25.95 mi | 33.86 mi | +1.0 |\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\n| Total time | 5h 20m | 4h 4m | 5h 15m | +5m |\\n| Total elevation | 722 ft | 525 ft | 741 ft | -20 ft |\\n| Relative effort | 274 | 171 | 241 | +33 |\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 143 | 144 | +0 |\\n\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\n\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.3%   (4h 17m)\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  12.1%   (39m)\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.4%   (21m)\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\n\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.51%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\n\\n## Run-by-run\\n\\n### Tue Sep 22 — Easy Run — 5.16 mi / 48m 4s\\n\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max 