% Z3 last week.", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "quality", "shoes": "Saucony Endorphin Speed 4", "paceOrHr": "Tempo 8:15 – 8:25/mi, WU/CD ~9:45/mi", "distanceM": 8047, "structure": "2 mi WU, 2 mi tempo @ 8:15 – 8:25/mi, 1 mi CD"}, "date": "2026-09-24", "notes": "First tempo back. Small on purpose — 8:15 – 8:25/mi, not MP. Stop if the Achilles sharpens with pace.", "dayType": "quality"}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "notes": "Fixed rest. Second strength session if you are home.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:50 – 10:00/mi", "distanceM": 8047, "structure": "5 mi steady easy"}, "date": "2026-09-26", "notes": "Easy hour before Sunday. If legs feel flat after Thursday, drop to 4 miles — no hero stuff.", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "long", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 152", "distanceM": 19312, "structure": "12 mi continuous easy"}, "date": "2026-09-27", "notes": "Steady 12, no MP finish. Fuel at ~45 and ~90 minutes with water, keep HR under 152 through mile 8.", "dayType": "long"}], "week": "2026-W39"}}, {"isoWeek": "2026-W38", "analysis": "## Why this shape\\n\\nYou stopped Thursday's session because the Achilles got sharper with pace, and Saturday it was stiff for a mile before settling. That is the classic early-warning pattern and the right response is a short, soft week — not a lost block. The race is nine weeks out and your aerobic base is in good shape, so losing a sharpening week costs you nothing.\\n\\nQuality is out this week. Pace changes and push-off load the Achilles the most, and that is exactly what provoked it. We hold easy aerobic running at flat routes only, and skip the Thursday hill loop.\\n\\n## How to run this week\\n\\nUse a simple traffic-light rule each day. Pain under 2/10 that eases in the first mile and does not get worse while running: go. Pain 3/10 or climbing during the run: stop and walk home. Any sharp pain, swelling, or morning limp: do not run and get it looked at.\\n\\nShoes stay in the Ghost 16 all week — more stack, less heel drop stress than the Speed 4. Skip calf raises and anything that loads the Achilles hard until a professional clears you. Short, gentle walking is fine and helpful.\\n\\n## What's next\\n\\nIf the Achilles settles cleanly by Sunday, next week we rebuild to a normal easy week and then layer quality back in the week after. If it is still grumbling, we hold easy or cross-train longer. Nine weeks is enough runway to protect this and still run 3:30 — pushing through it now is what turns a tight tendon into a six-week problem.", "recapMarkdown": "# Weekly Recap — 2026-W38 (Mon Sep 14 – Sun Sep 20, 2026)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Mileage | 25.95 mi | 31.22 mi | 36.45 mi | -10.5 |\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\n| Total time | 4h 4m | 4h 51m | 5h 39m | -1h 35m |\\n| Total elevation | 525 ft | 745 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\n\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\n\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\n\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\n\\n## Run-by-run\\n\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\n\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\n\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\n\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\n\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\n\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\n\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\n\\nRelative effort: 27\\n\\nSimilar route: n/a\\n\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\n\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\n\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\n\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\n\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\n\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\n\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\n\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\n\\nRelative effort: 32\\n\\nSimilar route: n/a\\n\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\n\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\n\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\n\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\n\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\n\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\n\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\n\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\n\\nRelative effort: 33\\n\\nSimilar route: n/a\\n\\nNotes (from app): \\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\"\\n\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\n\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\n\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\n\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\n\\nHR drift: 137.9 → 143.2 (+5.3 bpm)\\n\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\n\\nElevation: ↑112 ft\\n\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\n\\nRelative effort: 27\\n\\nSimilar route: n/a\\n\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\n\\n### Sun Sep 20 — Long Run — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\n\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\n\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\n\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\n\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.7% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\n\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\n\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\n\\nRelative effort: 52\\n\\nSimilar route: n/a\\n\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\n\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 20 — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\n\\nAvg pace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\n\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\n\\nBack half avg pace: 9:18/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\n\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\n\\n## Trends\\n\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi ▁▃██\\n\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 143 ▁▁▁█\\n\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi ▃█▃▁\\n\\n## Subjective recap\\n\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 6.9–8.2)\\n\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2 (Calf raises and slow heel drops.)\\n\\nStress level: Low. Easier at work.\\n\\nBody check: The Achilles is a lot better. Nothing at all on Saturday or Sunday, and not stiff afterwards. Saw a sports physio on Wednesday: mild Achilles tendinopathy, nothing torn. She cleared me to keep running, gave me slow heel drops twice a day, and said one short tempo next week is fine if the morning stiffness stays gone.\\n\\nGoing into next week feeling: Better. Frustrated about the missing miles but I can live with it.\\n\\n## Questions for coach\\n\\n1. The physio is happy for me to try a short tempo next week. Can we put one in?\\n2. Does the missed week change what is realistic for race day?\\n", "weekSessionId": "b992919d-3a13-4d00-bfe2-bff4ac590b02", "prescribedWeek": {"days": [{"date": "2026-09-14", "notes": "Fixed rest and travel. Book a physio appointment today if you can.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 148", "distanceM": 4828, "structure": "3 mi easy on flat pavement"}, "date": "2026-09-15", "notes": "Short test run. If Achilles is above 2/10 or sharpens, stop and walk back — no heroics.", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "paceOrHr": "9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 150", "distanceM": 6437, "structure": "4 mi flat easy"}, "date": "2026-09-16", "notes": "Only if Tuesday ran clean. Flat loop, steady, no pickups.", "dayType": "easy", "strength": "Skip calf/Achilles loading this week. Hips and core only, light."}, {"date": "2026-09-17", "notes": "Extra rest instead of the usual Thursday quality. The tendon needs the recovery window more than the session.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"date": "2026-09-18", "notes": "Fixed rest, travel day. Walk a bit; keep moving gently.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:50 – 10:10/mi", "distanceM": 6437, "structure": "4 mi flat easy"}, "date": "2026-09-19", "notes": "Easy flat miles. Skip if the Achilles was worse during the week.", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "long", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 150", "distanceM": 12875, "structure": "8 mi steady easy on flat pavement"}, "date": "2026-09-20", "notes": "Short long run, all easy, no MP finish. Cut to 6 if any Achilles signal in the first mile.", "dayType": "long"}], "week": "2026-W38"}}], "prescribedWeek": {"days": [{"date": "2026-10-12", "notes": "Fixed rest and travel. Walk, hydrate, bed early — the 20 miler is still in your legs.", "dayType": "rest"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 148", "distanceM": 8047, "structure": "5 mi steady easy on flat pavement"}, "date": "2026-10-13", "notes": "Easy opener. First mile at 9:40/mi, no pace chasing — HR sets the ceiling.", "dayType": "easy"}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 150", "distanceM": 11265, "structure": "7 mi steady easy"}, "date": "2026-10-14", "notes": "Midweek aerobic. Keep this in Z2 — it kept leaking to Z3 last week.", "dayType": "easy", "strength": "Short strength: hips, core, heel drops."}, {"run": {"type": "easy", "shoes": "Brooks Ghost 16", "paceOrHr": "9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 148", "distanceM": 6437, "structure": "4 mi steady easy on flat pavement"}, "date": "2026-10-15", "notes": "Short easy to fit the 40-minute wi