om where I am now?\\\\n\\"}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W35\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-08-24T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-08-31T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-08-24\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-08-30\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgTqdrrvaETgRPDKKkjgV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Given how big that last week was, with high stress and poor sleep stacking up, I'm thinking this should be a cutback week—around 34-36 miles, a shorter long run of 12-13, and simpler quality work like strides instead of hard efforts, keeping the easy days truly easy. I also need to address how to handle missed runs given upcoming travel, and I'm starting to sketch out the week starting Monday 8/24 with a rest day followed by an easy Tuesday.\\n\\nFilling out the rest of the week: easy Wednesday, a lighter quality session Thursday (settling on 2mi warmup, 3x1mi at marathon pace with 2min jogs, plus cooldown for about 6mi given the fatigue), rest Friday, easy Saturday, and a 12-mile long run Sunday—totaling about 35 miles, a solid step down from the previous 42.55.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AoSxKTnZFC9hxMKcdo8frL","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"headline":"Last week was a big jump on tired legs and short sleep, so this week pulls mileage back about 15% and keeps the quality light while the long run holds.","flags":[{"title":"Cutback week","detail":"Mileage drops from 42.5 to around 35. You asked for a lighter week and the numbers back it up."},{"title":"Sleep and stress","detail":"6.4 hr average with high work stress. If sleep stays under 6 hr, swap Thursday's reps for easy miles."},{"title":"Long-run drift","detail":"Sunday drifted +7.3 bpm over 15 miles. Start slower this Sunday and keep HR under 150 through mile 8."},{"title":"Strength","detail":"One of two done last week. Aim for both short sessions; skip rather than squeeze a late evening one."}],"answers":[{"question":"My schedule gets tight when I travel for work. How should I handle missed runs?","answer":"Protect the long run and one quality session; drop easy miles first.\\n\\nMy priority order when a travel week compresses:\\n\\n| Priority | Keep | Why |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| 1 | Sunday long run | Biggest marathon-specific stimulus. Move it to Saturday if Sunday is a travel day. |\\n| 2 | One quality session | Keeps goal pace in the legs. Shorten rather than skip — three MP miles is still useful. |\\n| 3 | Easy aerobic time | Nice to have. A 30-minute hotel treadmill run counts. |\\n\\nDo not try to make up missed miles the following week — stacking a travel week with a catch-up week is how the shin trouble came back last time. If you lose two or more runs, treat the next week as a soft restart: easy days easy, long run no more than last completed long plus a mile."}],"analysis":"## Why a cutback now\\n\\nYou jumped 7 miles week over week on 6.4 hours of sleep and high work stress, and Saturday's easy run already felt like work. That is the moment to pull back a notch, not push through. The pattern we want in a build is three up, one down, and you have had three up weeks in a row.\\n\\n## What stays, what shrinks\\n\\nLong run holds near 12 miles so you keep the aerobic stimulus but with less total load around it. Thursday's workout drops to three marathon-pace miles with full recoveries — enough to touch 8:00/mi cleanly without the Z4 time you got from the longer tempo. Easy days stay the same length but I want them genuinely easy, HR under 150, pace closer to 9:50 than 9:30.\\n\\n## Looking ahead\\n\\nIf this week lands well, next week goes back up toward 40 with a 16-mile long run and a longer quality session. If sleep stays short or anything in the shins whispers, we hold flat another week — the race is still 11 weeks out and the base is there.","prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W35","days":[{"date":"2026-08-24","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest with travel. Short walk and some hip mobility if you have 10 minutes."},{"date":"2026-08-25","dayType":"easy","notes":"Easy opener. First mile deliberately slow — let HR settle before you find a rhythm.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"9:50 – 10:00/mi, HR under 148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"5 mi steady easy"}},{"date":"2026-08-26","dayType":"easy","notes":"Standard mid-week easy. Keep it in Z2 — this one has crept into Z3 twice recently.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":11265,"paceOrHr":"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 150","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"7 mi steady easy"}},{"date":"2026-08-27","dayType":"quality","notes":"Short goal-pace reps with full recovery. Enough to feel 8:00/mi without draining the week.","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":9656,"paceOrHr":"MP 8:00/mi, recoveries 10:00/mi","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4","structure":"2 mi WU · 3 x 1 mi at 8:00/mi w/ 2 min easy jog · 1 mi CD"}},{"date":"2026-08-28","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest. Good day for the second short strength session if you are home."},{"date":"2026-08-29","dayType":"easy","notes":"Easy hour before Sunday. If legs feel flat, cut to 4 miles — no hero stuff.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"9:50 – 10:00/mi","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"5 mi steady easy"}},{"date":"2026-08-30","dayType":"long","notes":"Steady 12. Start before sunrise, carry fluid, hold HR under 150 through mile 8 then let it climb naturally.","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":19312,"paceOrHr":"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 152","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"12 mi steady, no MP finish"}}]}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":14562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens