· Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 36\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 23 — Long Run — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73.6% · Z3 26.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑420 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 103\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 23 — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:36/mi vs front 9:35/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.4 hrs (range 5.5–7.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Too tired Wednesday evening.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: High. Deadline at work, late nights Tuesday and Wednesday.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Tired more than sore. Saturday's easy run felt like work.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Hoping the next week eases off a bit.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. My schedule gets tight when I travel for work. How should I handle missed runs?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why this week looks the way it does\\\\n\\\\nYou handled 37.7 miles with an honest long run and the aerobic signal is clean, so the next step is a small build to about 40 with one controlled tempo. Easy HR has stayed at 144 while easy pace nudged from 9:50 to 9:43, which is exactly the direction you want for a marathon base.\\\\n\\\\nThursday is a tempo rather than reps because you flagged the 800s felt too fast early. Running sustained 4 miles near 8:15 – 8:25 per mile teaches pacing discipline and gives a cleaner read on where fitness sits versus 3:30 goal pace of 8:00/mi. The Endorphin Speed 4 is the right shoe for it.\\\\n\\\\nThe long run grows to 14 miles at the same easy effort you ran Sunday. If the air is thick at 6am again, drop pace by 10 – 20 seconds per mile from the start rather than hanging on and drifting late, which is what the +6.9 bpm drift on Sunday hinted at.\\\\n\\\\nMileage is up roughly 2 miles on last week, well inside a safe ramp given your shin history. Keep the two strength sessions in and the sleep closer to 7.5 if you can; it is the cheapest gain available right now.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day. Travel day, nothing to prove.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR 135 – 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy shakeout to open the week. Keep HR under 150 and let pace be whatever that is.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR 135 – 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-19\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Standard midweek aerobic run before Thursday's tempo. Nothing creeping into Z3.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\