n\\\\nElevation: ↑138 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 90\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 5 — Easy Run — 5.00 mi / 48m 12s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:41/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.8 → 143.6 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑118 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 6 — Long Run — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149 (79.3% max)  ·  Max HR 168  ·  Cad 346 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73% · Z3 19.1% · Z4 7.6% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑397 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 105\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 6 — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149  ·  Drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:07/mi vs front 9:25/mi (faster than front half by 18s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi ▁▁▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi ▃▅▁█\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.2 hrs (range 6.5–7.9)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low to moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs a little heavy after the long run, otherwise good.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Confident. Marathon pace felt controlled for the first time.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is it worth trying a gel on the long run next week, or keep it simple?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nLast week was a planned step back and you came out of it feeling bouncy, so this week rebuilds to around 42 miles with the long run going to 16 and one quality session touching marathon pace. You are 11 weeks out from Lakeshore, which is the right window to start layering goal-pace work into the long run instead of only doing it on Thursday.\\\\n\\\\n## The quality day\\\\n\\\\nThursday is marathon-pace reps: 2 x 3 miles at 8:00/mi with 3 minutes easy jog between. Two three-mile blocks are long enough to feel like race rhythm but short enough that you are not hanging on in the second half, which is where pacing errors show up. If 8:00 feels forced in the first rep, settle at 8:05 and we will tighten it over the next few weeks.\\\\n\\\\n## The long run\\\\n\\\\nSixteen miles Sunday, mostly steady, with the last 3 miles lifted to marathon-pace effort. This is the first time this block we are putting goal pace on tired legs, and it is the single most useful workout between here and taper. Start the first 10 miles honest and easy (9:40 – 9:55), then roll into 8:00 – 8:05 for the finish.\\\\n\\\\n## Easy running and context\\\\n\\\\nEasy pace has crept from 9:50 to 9:34 at the same 144 HR, which is exactly the aerobic drift you want. Keep Tue, Wed and Sat properly easy — if HR climbs toward 150 early, slow down. Fueling for the long runs matters more now that we are over two hours, and I have put specifics in the answer.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-31\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest with travel. Walk, hydrate, early night before Tuesday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35 – 9:50/mi, HR 135 – 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-01\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener. HR under 148, pace is whatever that gives you.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35 – 9:50/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-02\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Midweek aerobic run before Thursday's quality. Nothing creeping into Z3.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP 8:00/mi, recoveries ~10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU @ 9:45/mi, 2 x 3 mi @ 8:00/mi w/ 3 min easy jog, 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-03\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Marathon-pace reps. First real touch of 8:00/mi this block — settle in, do not force it.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-04\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Travel day. Eat and sleep well for Sunday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-05\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy hour on legs to set up Sunday. Properly easy, no chasing.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"First 13 mi 9:40 – 9:55/mi, last 3 mi 8:00 – 8:05/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":25750,\\"structure\\":\\"13 mi steady easy, then 3 mi at MP 8:00 – 8:05/mi (no CD needed)\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-06\\",\\"notes\\":\\"16 mi with last 3 at MP. First MP-on-tired-legs rep. Start honest, finish strong — fuel plan in the answer.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W36\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W35\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"f71bdae7-2e7c-4e9b-9573-875357c99847\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W35 (Mon Aug 24 – Sun Aug 30, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 33.72 mi | 42.55 mi | 38.69 mi | -5.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 18m | 6h 44m | 6h 8m | -49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 587 ft | 988 ft | 832 ft | -245 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 271 | 342 | 312 | -41 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80%   (4h 15m)\\\\nZ3 ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  15.9%   (51m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.7%   (9m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.45%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 25 — Easy Run — 5.04 mi / 48m 15s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:35/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 143.9 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑105 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 26 — Easy Run — 6.92 mi / 1h 5m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:30/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.2 → 150 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 92.4% · Z3 7.6% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 46\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 27 — Interval Run — 5.99 mi / 52m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 153 (80.9% max)  ·  Max HR 176  ·  Cad 349 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:39/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:41/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:34/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 140.2 → 146.3 (+6.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.8% · Z2 35.7% · Z3 44.4% · Z4 16.1% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 85\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 29 — Easy Run — 4.90 mi / 47m 18s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:39/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:36/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.9 → 144.4 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑79 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 30 — Long Run — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑187 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 73\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 30 — 10.86 mi / 1h 44m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.6 (+8.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:31/mi vs front 9:28/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi ▁▃▃█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi ▃▅█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8.1)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Deadline done.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Best I've felt in a month. Legs have some bounce again.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Ready to go again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. What should I be eating and drinking on the long runs? I've mostly gone without so far.\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why a cutback now\\\\n\\\\nYou jumped 7 miles week over week on 6.4 hours of sleep and high work stress, and Saturday's easy run already felt like work. That is the moment to pull back a notch, not push through. The pattern we want in a build is three up, one down, and you have had three up weeks in a row.\\\\n\\\\n## What stays, what shrinks\\\\n\\\\nLong run holds near 12 miles so you keep the aerobic stimulus but with less total load around it. Thursday's workout drops to three marathon-pace miles with full recoveries — enough to touch 8:00/mi cleanly without the Z4 time you got from the longer tempo. Easy days stay the same length but I want them genuinely easy, HR under 150, pace closer to 9:50 than 9:30.\\\\n\\\\n## Looking ahead\\\\n\\\\nIf this week lands well, next week goes back up toward 40 with a 16-mile long run and a longer quality session. If sleep stays short or anything in the shins whispers, we hold flat another week — the race is still 11 weeks out and the base is there.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest with travel. Short