ute: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 20 — Tempo Run — 8.14 mi / 1h 11m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 173  ·  Cad 352 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 7:47/mi / 7:39/mi / 7:45/mi / 7:42/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 140.3 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 53.3% · Z3 5.6% · Z4 38.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑223 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 108\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 22 — Easy Run — 5.18 mi / 50m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 345 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:52/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.2 → 143.9 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2% · Z2 98% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 36\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 23 — Long Run — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73.6% · Z3 26.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑420 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 103\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 23 — 15.17 mi / 2h 26m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144 → 151.3 (+7.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:36/mi vs front 9:35/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.4 hrs (range 5.5–7.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Too tired Wednesday evening.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: High. Deadline at work, late nights Tuesday and Wednesday.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Tired more than sore. Saturday's easy run felt like work.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Hoping the next week eases off a bit.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. My schedule gets tight when I travel for work. How should I handle missed runs?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why this week looks the way it does\\\\n\\\\nYou handled 37.7 miles with an honest long run and the aerobic signal is clean, so the next step is a small build to about 40 with one controlled tempo. Easy HR has stayed at 144 while easy pace nudged from 9:50 to 9:43, which is exactly the direction you want for a marathon base.\\\\n\\\\nThursday is a tempo rather than reps because you flagged the 800s felt too fast early. Running sustained 4 miles near 8:15 – 8:25 per mile teaches pacing discipline and gives a cleaner read on where fitness sits versus 3:30 goal pace of 8:00/mi. The Endorphin Speed 4 is the right shoe for it.\\\\n\\\\nThe long run grows to 14 miles at the same easy effort you ran Sunday. If the air is thick at 6am again, drop pace by 10 – 20 seconds per mile from the start rather than hanging on and drifting late, which is what the +6.9 bpm drift on Sunday hinted at.\\\\n\\\\nMileage is up roughly 2 miles on last week, well inside a safe ramp given your shin history. Keep the two strength sessions in and the sleep closer to 7.5 if you can; it is the cheapest gain available right now.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day. Travel day, nothing to prove.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR 135 – 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy shakeout to open the week. Keep HR under 150 and let pace be whatever that is.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR 135 – 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-19\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Standard midweek aerobic run before Thursday's tempo. Nothing creeping into Z3.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Tempo miles 8:15 – 8:25/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU @ 9:45/mi, 4 mi tempo @ 8:15 – 8:25/mi (one continuous block), 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Continuous tempo to practice pacing discipline after last week's fast 800s. Steady is the win here.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest day. Full recovery before the weekend double.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-22\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy hour on legs to set up Sunday. Properly easy, no pace chasing.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR 142 – 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"14 mi continuous easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Long run up to 14 mi at the same easy effort as last Sunday. If humid at 6am, start 10 – 20 sec/mi slower.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W34\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W33\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"fb524296-d5a5-481d-950c-93d942c0b4f7\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W33 (Mon Aug 10 – Sun Aug 16, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 37.74 mi | 35.77 mi | 33.43 mi | +4.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 57m | 5h 43m | 5h 25m | +32m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 764 ft | 664 ft | +81 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 304 | 289 | 244 | +60 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.3%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  79.8%   (4h 46m)\\\\nZ3 █████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  13.3%   (48m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  5.3%   (19m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0.3%   (1m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.07%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Aug 11 — Easy Run — 4.93 mi / 47m 57s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:44/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:44/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.5 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Aug 12 — Easy Run — 7.92 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:38/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:38/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.3 → 149.5 (+4.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.2% · Z3 9.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑138 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Aug 13 — Interval Run — 6.95 mi / 59m 12s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:32/mi  ·  Avg HR 154 (81.9% max)  ·  Max HR 180  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:43/mi / 9:41/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:36/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:41/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:39/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:38/mi / 9:46/mi / 9:51/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.8 → 143.5 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.4% · Z2 40% · Z3 22.8% · Z4 32.1% · Z5 1.7%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑92 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 95\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 8/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Aug 15 — Easy Run — 4.92 mi / 48m 22s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:49/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:44/mi / 9:47/mi / 9:44/mi / 9:54/mi / 9:43/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 143.9 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑108 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Aug 16 — Long Run — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.4% · Z2 78.4% · Z3 21.2% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑305 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 88\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 5/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Aug 16 — 13.03 mi / 2h 6m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:41/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 144.3 → 151.2 (+6.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:39/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:41/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:39/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:41/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:38/mi vs front 9:38/mi (vs front half; Δ -1s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:50/mi → 9:50/mi → 9:45/mi → 9:43/mi ▁▁▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 9.89 mi → 10.80 mi → 12.08 mi → 13.03 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.9 hrs (range 6–7.6)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: All fine. Sunday was a slog in the humidity but nothing hurts.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. A bit worried the 800s were too fast early on.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I slow the long run down when it is this hot, or hold the pace?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nLast week jumped about 10% in miles and the overall effort score climbed well above your 3-week average, so this week holds mileage flat and keeps the quality session shorter. You are healthy and the long run went well, but a second big jump on top of 25°C mornings is where shin trouble tends to creep back in.\\\\n\\\\n## The quality day\\\\n\\\\nThursday moves from a straight tempo to marathon-pace miles with full recoveries. Goal pace for 3:30 is 8:00/mi, and short reps let you touch that pace in the heat without the heart rate drift you would get from a long block. If 8:00 feels forced, run 8:05 – 8:10 and we will build from there.\\\\n\\\\n## Easy running\\\\n\\\\nKeep Tuesday, Wednesday and Saturday properly easy, which for you right now means roughly 9:45 – 10:00/mi and heart rate under 150. Your Wednesday run drifted into Z3 last week; start the first mile slower and let it settle.\\\\n\\\\n## Long run\\\\n\\\\nThirteen miles on Sunday, steady, no marathon-pace finish this week. Start before sunrise if you can, carry fluid, and if the heat index is brutal, cut it to 11 rather than grind.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest with travel. Walk and hydrate if you can.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:00/mi, HR 130 – 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy shakeout to open the week. Keep HR under 150 and start the first mile slow.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:00/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-12\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Standard mid-week easy. Last week this run drifted to Z3 — ease into it.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP 8:00/mi, recoveries 10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU · 5 x 1 mi at 8:00/mi w/ 2 min easy jog · 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Marathon-pace reps with full recovery. Short enough to hit goal pace cleanly in heat.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest for travel. Try to get the strength session in if you are home.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy hour, legs loose for Sunday. Nothing to prove.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 152\\",\\"distanceM\\":20921,\\"structure\\":\\"13 mi steady. Start before sunrise, carry fluid.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Steady 13 — small bump from last week. No MP finish; just time on feet in heat.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W33\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W38\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-14T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-09-21T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-09-20\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgTqpPtFNAUeefR7qSWd5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This sounds like a legitimate overuse injury flag since the tightness worsened with pace and forced a stop—I should recommend conservative management and professional evaluation rather than pushing through. I'm sketching a cutback week that swaps quality sessions for easy runs or cross-training, trims the long run, and keeps running contingent on pain staying low and stable, while laying out specific dates starting Monday the 14th.\\n\\nWith the race on Nov 15, there's nine weeks of buffer, so I can afford to be cautious now: rest Monday, test with a short easy run Tuesday, continue easy mileage if pain stays at 2 or below, avoid hills, and keep Sunday's long run easy without marathon pace work.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UGkeNYyFsp4tX8nDC18N1R","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"headline":"The Achilles signal from Thursday is the whole story this week — we pull quality out, keep running only if pain stays low and not worsening, and you get it looked at by a sports physio.","analysis":"## Why this shape\\n\\nYou stopped Thursday's session because the Achilles got sharper with pace, and Saturday it was stiff for a mile before settling. That is the classic early-warning pattern and the right response is a short, soft week — not a lost block. The race is nine weeks out and your aerobic base is in good shape, so losing a sharpening week costs you nothing.\\n\\nQuality is out this week. Pace changes and push-off load the Achilles the most, and that is exactly what provoked it. We hold easy aerobic running at flat routes only, and skip the Thursday hill loop.\\n\\n## How to run this week\\n\\nUse a simple traffic-light rule each day. Pain under 2/10 that eases in the first mile and does not get worse while running: go. Pain 3/10 or climbing during the run: stop and walk home. Any sharp pain, swelling, or morning limp: do not run and get it looked at.\\n\\nShoes stay in the Ghost 16 all week — more stack, less heel drop stress than the Speed 4. Skip calf raises and anything that loads the Achilles hard until a professional clears you. Short, gentle walking is fine and helpful.\\n\\n## What's next\\n\\nIf the Achilles settles cleanly by Sunday, next week we rebuild to a normal easy week and then layer quality back in the week after. If it is still grumbling, we hold easy or cross-train longer. Nine weeks is enough runway to protect this and still run 3:30 — pushing through it now is what turns a tight tendon into a six-week problem.","flags":[{"title":"Achilles — pain-dependent week","detail":"Right Achilles tightened with pace Thu and was stiff Sat. All quality pulled. Run only if pain stays under 2/10 and does not worsen."},{"title":"See a sports physio","detail":"Get it assessed early this week. Nine weeks to race gives time to fix it; another hard session on it does not."},{"title":"Shoes and routes","detail":"Ghost 16 only. Flat paved loops. Skip the Thursday hill route — climbs load the Achilles."},{"title":"No calf loading","detail":"Hold off heavy calf raises, jumps, strides, and sprints until you are cleared and pain-free running."}],"answers":[{"question":"Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?","answer":"Easy running is okay this week **only** if the Achilles behaves. Use this rule each run:\\n\\n| Pain during run | What to do |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Under 2/10, eases after first mile | Continue as planned |\\n| 3/10 or climbing | Stop and walk home |\\n| Sharp, or morning limp next day | Do not run, rest and get it assessed |\\n\\nI would also take Thursday as a second rest day this week to give it an extra 48-hour window. No pace changes, no hills, no strides. Short walks and gentle ankle mobility are fine. If two consecutive runs feel clean, we are on track to rebuild next week."},{"question":"How do I know if this is serious?","answer":"That is a question for a sports physio, not me — and I would book one this week rather than wait. I can't diagnose anything, but the pattern coaches watch for is: pain that sharpens with pace, morning stiffness that takes more than a few steps to clear, visible swelling or a lump on the tendon, pain when you press it, or pain going up stairs or doing a single-leg calf raise. Any of those earn a visit.\\n\\nThe reassuring signs are: tightness that eases within the first mile of easy running, no morning limp, no swelling, and settles with a day or two off. You are in a mixed picture right now, which is why we train conservatively and get professional eyes on it."}],"safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Get the Achilles assessed this week","body":"Pain that sharpens with pace and lingers as morning stiffness is worth a professional look, not a wait-and-see. Please book a sports physio or sports medicine doctor in the next few days — they can tell you what's going on and what loading is safe.\\n\\nStop running and seek same-day care if you get sudden sharp pain, a pop or snap sensation, visible swelling, or you can't push off the foot normally. I'm coaching the training around this; the medical read needs to come from a qualified professional.","severity":"caution"}],"prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W38","days":[{"date":"2026-09-14","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest and travel. Book a physio appointment today if you can."},{"date":"2026-09-15","dayType":"easy","notes":"Short test run. If Achilles is above 2/10 or sharpens, stop and walk back — no heroics.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":4828,"paceOrHr":"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 148","structure":"3 mi easy on flat pavement","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}},{"date":"2026-09-16","dayType":"easy","notes":"Only if Tuesday ran clean. Flat loop, steady, no pickups.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":6437,"paceOrHr":"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 150","structure":"4 mi flat easy"},"strength":"Skip calf/Achilles loading this week. Hips and core only, light."},{"date":"2026-09-17","dayType":"rest","notes":"Extra rest instead of the usual Thursday quality. The tendon needs the recovery window more than the session."},{"date":"2026-09-18","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest, travel day. Walk a bit; keep moving gently."},{"date":"2026-09-19","dayType":"easy","notes":"Easy flat miles. Skip if the Achilles was worse during the week.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":6437,"paceOrHr":"9:50 – 10:10/mi","structure":"4 mi flat easy","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}},{"date":"2026-09-20","dayType":"long","notes":"Short long run, all easy, no MP finish. Cut to 6 if any Achilles signal in the first mile.","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":12875,"paceOrHr":"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 150","structure":"8 mi steady easy on flat pavement","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}}]}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24595,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2713,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":342}},"diagnostics":null}	200	46522	tool_use	24595	2713	0	0	ok	\N	342
