/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:01/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:06/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:15/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:03/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 8:48/mi vs front 9:10/mi (faster than front half by 23s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi → 9:14/mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 143 → 144 → 144 ▁█▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi ▃▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (317) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (223) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 7–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs tired after the long run but nothing sore. Achilles quiet.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. The last three miles at marathon pace were hard but I could have held it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. How should the final weeks before the race look?\\\\n\\",\\"thread\\":[],\\"attachments\\":[],\\"week\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W40\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-09-28T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-10-05T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"8d1621a0-dfc2-47d7-ac36-0c58953ae4b1\\"},\\"recentHistory\\":[{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W39\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"2453cc65-d713-4a3d-b143-23203b4e72e5\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W39 (Mon Sep 21 – Sun Sep 27, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 34.83 mi | 25.95 mi | 33.86 mi | +1.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 20m | 4h 4m | 5h 15m | +5m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 722 ft | 525 ft | 741 ft | -20 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 274 | 171 | 241 | +33 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 143 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.3%   (4h 17m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  12.1%   (39m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.4%   (21m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.51%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 22 — Easy Run — 5.16 mi / 48m 4s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.5 → 144.1 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 23 — Easy Run — 6.86 mi / 1h 3m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:07/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.1 → 150.3 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 86.4% · Z3 13.6% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑240 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 45\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 24 — Tempo Run — 7.01 mi / 1h 1m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 150 (79.8% max)  ·  Max HR 174  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:35/mi / 7:35/mi / 7:39/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 138.7 (+2.6 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.5% · Z2 57.5% · Z3 6.5% · Z4 33.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑121 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 92\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles no issue.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 26 — Easy Run — 3.85 mi / 36m 18s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:23/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:18/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.4 → 143.2 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 97.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑30 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 25\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 27 — Long Run — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 76.1% · Z3 23.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑230 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 78\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 27 — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:12/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ +3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi ▁▅▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 143 → 144 ▁▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi █▃▁▃\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Nothing. I kept checking for the Achilles on the tempo and it was fine.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Relieved and ready to build again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is there anything I should keep doing for the Achilles through race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Where we are\\\\n\\\\nYou lost about a week of load but the aerobic base is intact. Easy pace is still 9:20 – 9:30/mi at HR 142 – 143, and the Sunday long run drifted a reasonable +8 bpm over 8 miles. That is a healthy platform to build from with eight weeks until Lakeshore.\\\\n\\\\n## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nThe physio cleared one short tempo, so Thursday is deliberately small: a 2-mile tempo at 8:15 – 8:25/mi, not marathon pace. Short enough to test the Achilles under load, long enough to feel like a workout. If morning stiffness returns at any point before Thursday, swap it for an easy 5.\\\\n\\\\nThe long run moves back to 12 miles at pure easy effort. No marathon pace finish this week — we need two clean weeks of tempo and long run before layering goal pace on tired legs again. If Sunday goes well, the week of Sep 28 goes to 14 and we start reintroducing MP work the week after.\\\\n\\\\n## Easy running\\\\n\\\\nThree of the four easy runs last week crept toward 9:17 – 9:20/mi. That is sharper than it needs to be in a rebuild week. Open every run at 10:00/mi for the first mile and let HR, not pace, decide the rest.\\\\n\\\\n## Keep doing\\\\n\\\\nTwice-daily heel drops, the two short strength sessions, and the pre-run stiffness check. If first-mile stiffness ever rises above a 3/10 or sharpens with pace, stop the run and tell me — that is the signal the physio gave you, and it is the right one.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest with travel. Heel drops morning and evening.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-22\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener. First mile at 10:00/mi — check stiffness as you go, let HR settle before finding rhythm.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Standard midweek aerobic. Keep it honest in Z2 — this run crept to 15% Z3 last week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Tempo 8:15 – 8:25/mi, WU/CD ~9:45/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU, 2 mi tempo @ 8:15 – 8:25/mi, 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"First tempo back. Small on purpose — 8:15 – 8:25/mi, not MP. Stop if the Achilles sharpens with pace.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-25\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Second strength session if you are home.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy hour before Sunday. If legs feel flat after Thursday, drop to 4 miles — no hero stuff.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 152\\",\\"distanceM\\":19312,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi continuous easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Steady 12, no MP finish. Fuel at ~45 and ~90 minutes with water, keep HR under 152 through mile 8.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W39\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W38\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"b992919d-3a13-4d00-bfe2-bff4ac590b02\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W38 (Mon Sep 14 – Sun Sep 20, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 25.95 mi | 31.22 mi | 36.45 mi | -10.5 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 4m | 4h 51m | 5h 39m | -1h 35m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 525 ft | 745 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.9 → 143.2 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑112 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 20 — Long Run — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.7% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 52\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 20 — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:18/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi ▁▃██\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 143 ▁▁▁█\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi ▃█▃▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 6.9–8.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2 (Calf raises and slow heel drops.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Easier at work.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: The Achilles is a lot better. Nothing at all on Saturday or Sunday, and not stiff afterwards. Saw a sports physio on Wednesday: mild Achilles tendinopathy, nothing torn. She cleared me to keep running, gave me slow heel drops twice a day, and said one short tempo next week is fine if the morning stiffness stays gone.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Better. Frustrated about the missing miles but I can live with it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. The physio is happy for me to try a short tempo next week. Can we put one in?\\\\n2. Does the missed week change what is realistic for race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nYou stopped Thursday's session because the Achilles got sharper with pace, and Saturday it was stiff for a mile before settling. That is the classic early-warning pattern and the right response is a short, soft week — not a lost block. The race is nine weeks out and your aerobic base is in good shape, so losing a sharpening week costs you nothing.\\\\n\\\\nQuality is out this week. Pace changes and push-off load the Achilles the most, and that is exactly what provoked it. We hold easy aerobic running at flat routes only, and skip the Thursday hill loop.\\\\n\\\\n## How to run this week\\\\n\\\\nUse a simple traffic-light rule each day. Pain under 2/10 that eases in the first mile and does not get worse while running: go. Pain 3/10 or climbing during the run: stop and walk home. Any sharp pain, swelling, or morning limp: do not run and get it looked at.\\\\n\\\\nShoes stay in the Ghost 16 all week — more stack, less heel drop stress than the Speed 4. Skip calf raises and anything that loads the Achilles hard until a professional clears you. Short, gentle walking is fine and helpful.\\\\n\\\\n## What's next\\\\n\\\\nIf the Achilles settles cleanly by Sunday, next week we rebuild to a normal easy week and then layer quality back in the week after. If it is still grumbling, we hold easy or cross-train longer. Nine weeks is enough runway to protect this and still run 3:30 — pushing through it now is what turns a tight tendon into a six-week problem.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest and travel. Book a physio appointment today if you can.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":4828,\\"structure\\":\\"3 mi easy on flat pavement\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short test run. If Achilles is above 2/10 or sharpens, stop and walk back — no heroics.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi flat easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Only if Tuesday ran clean. Flat loop, steady, no pickups.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Skip calf/Achilles loading this week. Hips and core only, light.\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Extra rest instead of the usual Thursday quality. The tendon needs the recovery window more than the session.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest, travel day. Walk a bit; keep moving gently.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi flat easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-19\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy flat miles. Skip if the Achilles was worse during the week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi steady easy on flat pavement\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short long run, all easy, no MP finish. Cut to 6 if any Achilles signal in the first mile.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W38\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W37\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"48424895-cef1-450a-ab68-121423204d3a\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W37 (Mon Sep 7 – Sun Sep 13, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 31.22 mi | 44.41 mi | 40.23 mi | -9.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 51m | 6h 49m | 6h 17m | -1h 26m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 955 ft | 843 ft | -98 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 225 | 328 | 314 | -89 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.5%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████████░░░░░  87.1%   (4h 14m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  9.3%   (27m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.1%   (6m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **88.64%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 8 — Easy Run — 6.03 mi / 56m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑167 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 39\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 9 — Easy Run — 8.20 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146.1 → 150.2 (+4.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.7% · Z3 9.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 10 — Tempo Run — 3.10 mi / 28m 1s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 145 (77.1% max)  ·  Max HR 177  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:36/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 133.5 → 169.4 (+35.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 7.1% · Z2 66% · Z3 5.4% · Z4 21.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑10 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Right Achilles tight from mile 2. Stopped at 3.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 3/10  ·  Pain: Right Achilles tight from about mile 2 of the session. Got sharper as I picked up the pace, so I stopped at 3 miles and walked home.\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 12 — Easy Run — 3.89 mi / 37m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:36/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 144 (+6.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.7% · Z2 97.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 5/10  ·  Pain: Achilles stiff for the first mile, eased after that. About a 3 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 13 — Long Run — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 79.7% · Z3 19.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 65\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: No pain while running. Stiff getting out of the car afterwards.\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 13 — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:16/mi vs front 9:18/mi (vs front half; Δ +2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi █▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7 hrs (range 6.2–7.7)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped the second one to rest the legs.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Worried about the Achilles.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Right Achilles, just above the heel. Tight and a bit tender to press. No swelling that I can see. It was fine until the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Anxious. I don't want to throw away the block over this.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\\\n2. How do I know if this is serious?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why a cutback now\\\\n\\\\nYou went from 33.7 miles to 44.4 in a single step, with a 16-mile long run that finished at marathon pace. That is a lot of new load in one week, and the +13.4 bpm drift on Sunday tells me the back half cost more than the pace suggests. A small pullback now protects the gains and keeps the shins quiet.\\\\n\\\\n## What I like\\\\n\\\\nMarathon pace on Thursday sat at 7:58 – 8:01/mi with an average HR of 153 and you called it a 6/10. That is the first clean read we have had on goal pace, and the fact that you felt controlled is the sentence I care about most. Easy pace has drifted from 9:43 to 9:30 at the same 144 HR, which is honest aerobic progress.\\\\n\\\\n## What this week does\\\\n\\\\nMileage lands near 38 with the long run at 14 and no marathon-pace finish. Thursday is four MP miles broken into reps so you touch 8:00/mi again without stacking two hard long efforts back to back. If next Sunday feels crisp, the week after we go back up — likely 16 again, this time with a longer MP block built in.\\\\n\\\\n## Easy running\\\\n\\\\nThe two easy days drifted into Z3 last week (Wed 19% Z3, long run 19% Z3). That is where cutback weeks earn their keep. Start the first mile at 10:00/mi or slower on every easy day and let HR, not pace, set the ceiling.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-07\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest with travel. Short walk and hip mobility if you have ten minutes.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:00/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-08\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener after a big week. First mile at 10:00/mi — do not chase pace, let HR settle.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-09\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Standard midweek aerobic. Keep this one in Z2 — it slid into Z3 last Wednesday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP 8:00/mi, recoveries 9:45 – 10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU · 4 x 1 mi at 8:00/mi w/ 2 min easy jog · 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"MP reps with short recoveries. Touch 8:00/mi again without stacking a second long MP block on Sunday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Good day for the second strength session if you are home.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-12\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy hour before Sunday. If legs feel flat, cut to 4 — no hero stuff.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 152\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"14 mi steady. One gel at ~45 min, one at ~90 min, with fluid.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Steady 14, no MP finish. Fuel at 45 and 90 minutes to start building the race-day habit.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W37\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W36\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"ba71dfa0-e641-49e5-ab16-05476f66eca8\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W36 (Mon Aug 31 – Sun Sep 6, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 44.41 mi | 33.72 mi | 38.00 mi | +6.4 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 49m | 5h 18m | 6h 0m | +49m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 955 ft | 587 ft | 773 ft | +182 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 328 | 271 | 306 | +22 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░  73.4%   (5h 1m)\\\\nZ3 ████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  22.6%   (1h 33m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.8%   (11m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **74.64%**. **Below** typical marathon base target (≥80% Z1+Z2).\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 1 — Easy Run — 5.91 mi / 56m 22s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:33/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:30/mi / 9:36/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:31/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:26/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑121 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 39\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 2 — Easy Run — 9.18 mi / 1h 26m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 149 (79.3% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:25/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146.3 → 151 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 80.9% · Z3 19.1% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑180 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 60\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 3 — Marathon Pace Run — 8.22 mi / 1h 9m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:29/mi  ·  Avg HR 153 (81.4% max)  ·  Max HR 163  ·  Cad 356 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:35/mi / 9:31/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:56/mi / 7:56/mi / 8:01/mi / 8:01/mi / 8:01/mi / 9:43/mi / 9:39/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 141.8 → 148.9 (+7.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.6% · Z2 28.1% · Z3 68.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑138 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 90\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 5 — Easy Run — 5.00 mi / 48m 12s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:38/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:41/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:38/mi / 9:35/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.8 → 143.6 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑118 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 6 — Long Run — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149 (79.3% max)  ·  Max HR 168  ·  Cad 346 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 73% · Z3 19.1% · Z4 7.6% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑397 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 105\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 6/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 6 — 16.10 mi / 2h 29m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 149  ·  Drift: 143.5 → 156.9 (+13.4 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:58/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:07/mi vs front 9:25/mi (faster than front half by 18s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:43/mi → 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi ▁▁▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 13.03 mi → 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi ▃▅▁█\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.2 hrs (range 6.5–7.9)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low to moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs a little heavy after the long run, otherwise good.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Confident. Marathon pace felt controlled for the first time.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is it worth trying a gel on the long run next week, or keep it simple?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nLast week was a planned step back and you came out of it feeling bouncy, so this week rebuilds to around 42 miles with the long run going to 16 and one quality session touching marathon pace. You are 11 weeks out from Lakeshore, which is the right window to start layering goal-pace work into the long run instead of only doing it on Thursday.\\\\n\\\\n## The quality day\\\\n\\\\nThursday is marathon-pace reps: 2 x 3 miles at 8:00/mi with 3 minutes easy jog between. Two three-mile blocks are long enough to feel like race rhythm but short enough that you are not hanging on in the second half, which is where pacing errors show up. If 8:00 feels forced in the first rep, settle at 8:05 and we will tighten it over the next few weeks.\\\\n\\\\n## The long run\\\\n\\\\nSixteen miles Sunday, mostly steady, with the last 3 miles lifted to marathon-pace effort. This is the first time this block we are putting goal pace on tired legs, and it is the single most useful workout between here and taper. Start the first 10 miles honest and easy (9:40 – 9:55), then roll into 8:00 – 8:05 for the finish.\\\\n\\\\n## Easy running and context\\\\n\\\\nEasy pace has crept from 9:50 to 9:34 at the same 144 HR, which is exactly the aerobic drift you want. Keep Tue, Wed and Sat properly easy — if HR climbs toward 150 early, slow down. Fueling for the long runs matters more now that we are over two hours, and I have put specifics in the answer.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-08-31\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest with travel. Walk, hydrate, early night before Tuesday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35 – 9:50/mi, HR 135 – 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-01\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener. HR under 148, pace is whatever that gives you.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35 – 9:50/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-02\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Midweek aerobic run before Thursday's quality. Nothing creeping into Z3.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP 8:00/mi, recoveries ~10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU @ 9:45/mi, 2 x 3 mi @ 8:00/mi w/ 3 min easy jog, 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-03\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Marathon-pace reps. First real touch of 8:00/mi this block — settle in, do not force it.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-04\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Travel day. Eat and sleep well for Sunday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-05\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy hour on legs to set up Sunday. Properly easy, no chasing.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"First 13 mi 9:40 – 9:55/mi, last 3 mi 8:00 – 8:05/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":25750,\\"structure\\":\\"13 mi steady easy, then 3 mi at MP 8:00 – 8:05/mi (no CD needed)\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-06\\",\\"notes\\":\\"16 mi with last 3 at MP. First MP-on-tired-legs rep. Start honest, finish strong — fuel plan in the answer.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W36\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W41\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-10-05T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-10-12T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-10-05\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-10-11\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "xhigh"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgTrGQkZYYhLsADFqZJZP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This week jumped to 43.98 miles, a big leap over the prior week and three-week average, with a 17.18-mile long run finishing three miles at marathon pace. Heart rate drift ran high at +15.9 bpm above target, and relative effort hit 317, signaling this was a notably demanding week.\\n\\nWith the race set for Nov 15 and the next week starting Oct 5, I'm counting six weeks of training remaining, putting the athlete right at the peak training window. Given the sharp 42% mileage jump and 44% long-run jump, plus the overload and HR drift flags, I'm thinking this coming week calls for a cutback or at least a plateau rather than another big push — classic periodization suggests easing the load after a week like this.\\n\\nSketching out the six weeks: a step-back week first (~35-38 mi, long run 13-14 with light MP), then a peak week (~45 mi, long run 18-20 with MP), another strong quality week, then tapering down through race week. I'm weighing whether to squeeze in one more peak week before the taper begins.\\n\\nNow I'm factoring in the athlete's actual schedule — rest Mondays and Fridays for travel, running Tuesday through Thursday plus weekends, with weekday runs kept to about an hour and done early.\\n\\nTotaling that out gives about 39 miles, a roughly 10% cutback from 44, since that 17-mile long run really beat me up with the heart rate drift. I'll keep Thursday's quality session more modest — maybe 4 miles at MP instead of the longer block — and drop the long run to 14 with the last 4 at marathon pace.\\n\\nOn pacing, easy runs drifted to 9:14/mi which is too sharp; I want to pull that back to 9:30-9:50, and marathon pace target stays around 8:00/mi. The main flags this week are the long run heart rate drift, the easy pace creep, the mileage jump, and the relative effort signal — all pointing toward consolidating before the heaviest two weeks of the block. Now I'm sketching out the final six-week structure from Oct 5 to Nov 15, mapping mileage, long run, and quality work week by week.\\n\\nI also need to avoid certain flagged internal terms and stylistic habits like exclamation marks or sentences starting with \\"Let's\\" — I'll phrase things plainly instead, saying \\"during the week\\" rather than referencing a specific weekday shorthand.\\n\\nFor the Thursday workout, I want something that still touches marathon pace but is less taxing than a long continuous MP block paired with a big long run — maybe cruise intervals or shorter MP segments, like a short warmup followed by mile repeats at goal pace.\\n\\nFor Sunday, I'm leaning toward a cutback long run around 14 miles with the last stretch at MP, weighing whether tired legs from Thursday's reps make that finish valuable or unnecessary.\\n\\nLet me reconsider the volume — maybe dial back Thursday to 3 reps instead of 4, and keep Sunday's MP finish shorter too, so the weekly MP exposure doesn't creep up too fast.\\n\\nGoing with: Thursday 7mi (2 WU, 4x1mi MP w/ jog recovery, 1 CD), Sunday 14mi (11 easy + 3 MP). That's 7 total MP miles, slightly less than last week but better distributed. For shoes, Ghost 16 for easy days, Endorphin Speed 4 for Thursday's quality work, and Ghost 16 again for the long run.\\n\\nI should also flag the +15.9 bpm heart rate drift from last week's long run — that's a sign the late pace was too aggressive or fueling/hydration needs attention. Strength training went 2 for 2 last week, so I'll keep that pattern on Monday or Friday at home. For easy pace, HR cap is 150 and last week crept to 9:14/mi at HR 144 — still fine zone-wise but faster than necessary, so I'll suggest 9:30-9:50/mi instead. Now I'm drafting the day-by-day schedule starting with Monday as a rest/travel day.\\n\\nTotaling it up, this week lands at 39 miles, a clear step down after the recent peak. I want my analysis to cover why we're backing off now, why the long run shrinks to 14, the structure behind Thursday's mile repeats at marathon-adjacent pace, and a reminder on keeping easy days truly easy — saving the broader build-up roadmap for the actual answer rather than the analysis.\\n\\nLooking at the flags: the long run's heart rate drift (+15.9bpm) last Sunday points to pacing the start more conservatively, easy-day pace has crept too sharp at 9:14/mi for 144bpm, and the jump of 13 miles in a single week justifies this pullback as we move into peak phase six weeks out.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Looking at this week carefully:\\n- Mileage jumped from 30 → 44 (+13 mi, flagged as overload)\\n- Long run was 17 mi with MP finish, drift +15.9bpm (above target)\\n- Thursday MP run went well (8:00/mi, 6/10 effort)\\n- Athlete feels good, \\"could have held\\" MP\\n- Race is 6 weeks out (Nov 15)\\n- Question about final weeks structure\\n\\nStrategy: Consolidate this week before the two biggest weeks of the block (Oct 12-25), then taper. Drop long run to 14 (with 3 at MP), break Thursday MP into shorter reps, keep easy work truly easy."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YbfD2r7oqNWqtvvPZgdLva","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"headline":"After the biggest week in months, we consolidate at 39 miles with a 14-mile long run and shorter marathon-pace reps, so you arrive at the two peak weeks of Oct 12 – 25 fresh instead of fried.","analysis":"## Why we are stepping back\\n\\nYou jumped from 30 to 44 miles in one week with a 17-mile long run that finished at goal pace. That is a lot of new load, and the long-run drift of +15.9 bpm is the one line in your week I want to respect. The legs felt good on Monday, which is exactly why now is the time to consolidate, not keep piling on.\\n\\n## Why 14 miles on Sunday\\n\\nThe next two weeks are where the block earns the race, and both will carry 18 – 20 mile long runs with longer marathon-pace blocks. Running 15 or 16 this week would spend fitness I need you to have on Oct 18 and Oct 25. Fourteen with a 3-mile marathon-pace finish keeps you in rhythm without stacking two heavy Sundays back to back.\\n\\n## About that drift\\n\\nFifteen bpm over 17 miles usually means one of three things: opening pace was a touch quick, fueling was late, or the MP finish ran hot. Your front half was 9:10/mi which is honest, so my best guess is the MP miles pulled the average up. On Sunday, set a hard rule: no faster than 9:45/mi for the first two miles, and the MP block starts at 8:05, not 8:00.\\n\\n## Thursday as reps, not a block\\n\\nFour one-mile reps at 8:00/mi gives you the same seven miles of session volume as last Thursday but with recovery jogs built in. That means less cumulative fatigue going into Sunday while still rehearsing the pace. If the first rep feels forced, settle at 8:05 — we have four weeks of harder MP work ahead and nothing is proven today.\\n\\n## Easy days\\n\\nEasy pace drifted to 9:14/mi last week at HR 144. The HR is fine, the pace is sharper than you need. Start the first mile at 9:50 or slower on every easy day, let HR settle, and let that decide the rest. The point of easy days this week is to arrive at Thursday and Sunday with legs that want to work.","flags":[{"title":"Long-run drift above target","detail":"Sunday climbed +15.9 bpm over 17 miles. Open the next long run at 9:45/mi and start the MP block at 8:05, not 8:00."},{"title":"Easy pace creeping sharp","detail":"Easy days drifted to 9:14/mi at HR 144. First mile of every easy run opens at 9:50/mi, let HR set the ceiling."},{"title":"Big mileage jump","detail":"30 to 44 miles in one week is a lot. Cutting to 39 this week to protect the next two peak weeks."},{"title":"Six weeks to Lakeshore","detail":"Peak load lands Oct 12 – 25, then a three-week taper. Sleep and strength matter more every week from here."}],"answers":[{"question":"How should the final weeks before the race look?","answer":"Here is the shape I am aiming for between now and Nov 15. Numbers will adjust to how each week lands, but the arc is set.\\n\\n| Week | Miles | Long run | Quality focus |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Oct 5 – 11 | ~39 | 14 w/ last 3 at MP | 4 x 1 mi at MP |\\n| Oct 12 – 18 | ~46 | 18 w/ last 5 at MP | 2 x 3 mi at MP |\\n| Oct 19 – 25 | ~44 | 20 w/ 6 miles of MP mixed in | 4 mi continuous at MP |\\n| Oct 26 – Nov 1 | ~36 | 15 steady, no MP finish | 3 mi tempo |\\n| Nov 2 – 8 | ~28 | 10 w/ 3 at MP | Short MP strides |\\n| Nov 9 – 15 | ~16 + race | 4 mi shakeout Sat | Race Sun Nov 15 |\\n\\nThe two weeks of Oct 12 – 25 are the ones that matter most. Oct 18 is your biggest confidence long run — 18 miles with a five-mile marathon-pace block will tell us if 3:30 is the right target or if we dial to 3:32 – 3:34. Oct 25 is the longest session of the whole block at 20 miles, and after that we taper and you only need to not undo the work.\\n\\nTwo rules for the taper: miles come down, intensity stays. You will feel sluggish in the week of Nov 2 and that is normal — it is the taper, not lost fitness. Protect sleep, keep fueling the long runs, and we will talk race-day pacing and warm-up specifics around Nov 2."}],"prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W41","days":[{"date":"2026-10-05","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest, travel day. Walk if you can, light hip and ankle mobility in the evening."},{"date":"2026-10-06","dayType":"easy","notes":"Easy opener after Sunday's long effort. First mile at 9:50/mi, let HR settle before finding rhythm.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":9656,"paceOrHr":"9:35 – 9:50/mi, HR under 148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"6 mi steady easy"}},{"date":"2026-10-07","dayType":"easy","notes":"Standard aerobic hour before Thursday. Keep this one honest in Z2 — it crept to Z3 last week.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":11265,"paceOrHr":"9:30 – 9:45/mi, HR under 150","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"7 mi steady easy"}},{"date":"2026-10-08","dayType":"quality","notes":"Marathon-pace reps instead of a continuous block. Shorter pieces this week protects Sunday — settle at 8:05 if 8:00 feels forced.","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":11265,"paceOrHr":"MP 8:00/mi, recoveries ~9:45/mi","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4","structure":"2 mi WU @ 9:45/mi, 4 x 1 mi @ 8:00/mi w/ 2 min easy jog, 1 mi CD"}},{"date":"2026-10-09","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest, travel day. Good day for one strength session if you are home — hips, core, calves."},{"date":"2026-10-10","dayType":"easy","notes":"Easy hour on legs before Sunday. Properly easy — if legs feel flat, drop to 4 miles.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 148","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"5 mi steady easy"}},{"date":"2026-10-11","dayType":"long","notes":"14 with last 3 at MP. Open at 9:45/mi, do not touch 9:30 before mile 4, then roll into 8:00 – 8:05 for the finish. Fuel at 45 and 90 min.","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":22531,"paceOrHr":"First 11 mi 9:40 – 9:55/mi, last 3 mi 8:00 – 8:05/mi, HR under 152 through mile 8","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16","structure":"11 mi steady easy, then 3 mi at MP 8:00 – 8:05/mi"}}]}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24898,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7150,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4118}},"diagnostics":null}	200	102800	tool_use	24898	7150	0	0	ok	\N	4118
5b0fa021-c39e-44f5-a14d-805a8c3a7985	2026-10-11 20:01:26.005802+00	weekly_reply	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	199f5fbb-f5ad-4732-93ab-e9961070e6c3	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_weekly_reply", "description": "Submit the weekly coaching analysis and structured 7-day prescribed week.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["headline", "analysis", "prescribedWeek"], "properties": {"flags": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "detail"], "properties": {"title": {"type": "string", "description": "A few words, at most 80 characters."}, "detail": {"type": "string", "description": "One line, at most 280 characters."}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 5, "description": "What you are watching, not a summary of the week. Shown as a short list under \\"Watching\\"."}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["question", "answer"], "properties": {"answer": {"type": "string", "description": "Your answer, in markdown if it needs more than a paragraph."}, "question": {"type": "string", "description": "The athlete's question, quoted exactly as they wrote it."}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 8, "description": "One per question the athlete asked in the check-in or the conversation. Empty when they asked nothing."}, "analysis": {"type": "string", "description": "The rest of your read in markdown: your reasoning about the week and the plan. The athlete sees the headline, flags and answers above it."}, "headline": {"type": "string", "description": "One or two plain sentences, at most 280 characters: what you would say if you could say only one thing about the week and the plan. No markdown, no label."}, "prescribedWeek": {"type": "object", "required": ["week", "days"], "properties": {"days": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"], "description": "Why this session, this week: one or two sentences, under 200 characters. Shown beside the session."}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 7, "minItems": 7}, "week": {"type": "string", "description": "ISO week id, e.g. 2026-W43"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string", "maxLength": 600, "description": "At most 600 characters. One or two short paragraphs; the reply carries the detail."}, "title": {"type": "string", "maxLength": 120}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 5, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets (short)."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach producing a weekly training plan. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective, artifact, RPE, mid-week or prescribed. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\", \\"the plan\\", \\"how hard it felt\\" (or \\"effort 7/10\\"), \\"during the week\\" and \\"planned\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Week ids such as 2026-W43 are internal: never write them or a short form such as W43 or W43's. Name a week the way the athlete reads it: \\"this week\\", \\"next week\\", \\"the week of Oct 19\\", \\"Oct 19 – 25\\" or \\"4 weeks out from the race\\". Write plain sentences. No exclamation marks, no sentences that open with \\"Let's\\", and no emoji or decorative symbols. Write dates as \\"Mon Oct 19\\" and ranges as \\"Oct 19 – 25\\", never as 2026-10-19. Lead with the conclusion: the first sentence says what matters most. Give each paragraph one idea and state it in the paragraph's first sentence. Keep paragraphs to at most three sentences, and sentences under 25 words. When you give more than three numbers that belong together, such as splits, paces or heart rates, put them in a Markdown table instead of a sentence. Keep your reasoning as sentences: say why, not just what. The headline is the sentence you would say if you could say only one thing about the week and the plan: one or two plain sentences, no label. Flags are what you are watching, not a summary of the week: at most five, each a few-word title and one line of detail. Choose flags by what the athlete needs to act on. A correction comes first: when the athlete ran a session differently from the plan, flag it, and explain in the analysis what happened and why it matters. Answers are one per question the athlete asked in the weekly check-in or the conversation, with the question quoted exactly as they wrote it. When they asked nothing, leave answers empty. Put the reason for each session in that day's notes: one or two sentences on why this session, this week, under 200 characters. The athlete sees them beside the session. The athlete reads the headline, then the flags, then the answers, then the analysis, and the analysis may be folded away. Make each flag and answer stand on its own: never point to something \\"above\\" or \\"below\\", or to a table in another part. The analysis holds your reasoning. Do not restate the headline, flags or answers in it, and never repeat an answer's table or list there. Do not list the days or describe each session in it, as a list or as a table; the day rows already show them. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep each callout body under 600 characters: one or two short paragraphs. - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. Think it through first, then call the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reviewed week (already happened): 2026-W41\\nPlan week ISO label: 2026-W42\\nPlan week Monday (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-10-12\\nprescribedWeek.days must use these exact dates Mon–Sun: 2026-10-12, 2026-10-13, 2026-10-14, 2026-10-15, 2026-10-16, 2026-10-17, 2026-10-18\\nPrescribe one coherent week of running training for this athlete.\\nCall the submit_weekly_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nInclude a headline (the one or two sentences you would say if you could say only one thing), flags (what you are watching), answers (one per question the athlete asked, quoted as written) and the analysis (your reasoning).\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":1,\\"body\\":\\"# About you\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nYou are training for the Lakeshore Marathon on Sun Nov 15, aiming for 3:30. This will be your fourth marathon, and your personal best is 3:41 from two years ago.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nYou run five days a week: Tue, Wed, Thu, Sat and Sun. Mon and Fri are fixed rest days because of work travel.\\\\n\\\\nWeekday runs are early, around 6am before work, capped near an hour. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run.\\\\n\\\\nTypical volume is 6 to 7 hours a week, with more on long-run weeks.\\\\n\\\\n## Running history\\\\nYou have run three marathons already, best 3:41. You eased off in June and have built back to about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\nRecent weeks show four easy runs of roughly 5 to 6 miles and a long run of about 10.8 miles on Sun Aug 2.\\\\n\\\\n## Injuries and constraints\\\\nYou are healthy right now. You had shin splints in your first marathon block, so you prefer to ramp mileage up carefully.\\\\n\\\\nWork travel takes you away about one week in six. Mon and Fri rest days cannot move.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nYou train mostly on flat paved loops and a canal path, with one hillier route on Thursdays. You want easy days to be properly easy and you are happy to work hard on quality days.\\\\n\\\\nYou like to know why a session is in the plan. Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16 for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## Current status\\\\nYou are at about 30 miles a week with a long run near 11 miles. Units are miles. Heart rate zones are set custom, with easy running in 112 – 150 bpm.\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W41 (Mon Oct 5 – Sun Oct 11, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 44.97 mi | 43.98 mi | 34.92 mi | +10.1 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 40m | 6h 36m | 5h 20m | +1h 20m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 955 ft | 787 ft | 678 ft | +277 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 340 | 317 | 254 | +86 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (6m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░  67.3%   (4h 30m)\\\\nZ3 ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  16.7%   (1h 7m)\\\\nZ4 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  10.7%   (43m)\\\\nZ5 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  3.9%   (16m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **68.7%**. **Below** typical marathon base target (≥80% Z1+Z2).\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Oct 6 — Easy Run — 4.88 mi / 45m 7s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:15/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.6 → 143.9 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.3% · Z2 96.7% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑89 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Oct 7 — Easy Run — 7.94 mi / 1h 12m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:07/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146 → 149.8 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0