x long-typed, else max run in week): 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi ▃▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (317) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (223) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 7–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs tired after the long run but nothing sore. Achilles quiet.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. The last three miles at marathon pace were hard but I could have held it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. How should the final weeks before the race look?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nLast week was the first full load since the Achilles flare and it held together: tempo at 7:35/mi, long run at 9:18/mi with only +8.8 bpm drift, and no body-check flags. That earns a careful step up, not a leap. Seven weeks to race day means two more build weeks, then a peak block, then taper.\\\\n\\\\n## The quality day\\\\n\\\\nThursday is 2 x 2 miles at marathon pace with a 3-minute jog between. That is a longer continuous touch of 8:00/mi than the three Thursday tempo miles you ran last week, but still well short of the 8-mile MP session from early September. Stay on the flat canal loop, not the Thursday hills — pace changes and climbs are what loaded the tendon last time.\\\\n\\\\n## The long run\\\\n\\\\nFourteen miles Sunday with the last 2 at marathon pace. This is the first MP-on-tired-legs rep since the Achilles episode, kept deliberately short so you finish wanting more. If anything whispers in the tendon during the first 10 miles, drop the MP finish and jog it home — no points for toughing it out this far from the race.\\\\n\\\\n## Guardrails\\\\n\\\\nKeep the heel drops going daily, keep the Ghost 16 for everything except Thursday, and keep easy days honest (HR under 150). Wednesday drifted to 13.6% Z3 last week — fine, but let's keep it Z2 this week with Thursday getting harder.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest and travel. Heel drops morning and evening.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy on flat pavement\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-29\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener. First mile deliberately slow to let the tendon warm through.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:25 – 9:45/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-30\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Midweek aerobic. Keep this in Z2 — it drifted to Z3 last week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Short strength: hips, core, slow heel drops.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP 8:00/mi, recoveries 9:45/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":12070,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU · 2 x 2 mi at 8:00/mi w/ 3 min easy jog · 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-01\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Longer MP touch than last week, still short of September's tempo. Flat canal only — no hills.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-02\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest, travel. Walk, eat, sleep well for Sunday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30 – 9:50/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-03\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short easy hour on legs to set up Sunday. Properly easy.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Second strength session: heel drops, hips, core.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"First 12 mi 9:30 – 9:50/mi, last 2 mi 8:00 – 8:05/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi steady easy, then 2 mi at MP 8:00 – 8:05/mi\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-04\\",\\"notes\\":\\"14 mi with a short MP finish — first MP-on-tired-legs since the Achilles. Drop the MP if anything whispers in the first 10.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W40\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W39\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"2453cc65-d713-4a3d-b143-23203b4e72e5\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W39 (Mon Sep 21 – Sun Sep 27, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 34.83 mi | 25.95 mi | 33.86 mi | +1.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 20m | 4h 4m | 5h 15m | +5m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 722 ft | 525 ft | 741 ft | -20 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 274 | 171 | 241 | +33 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 143 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.3%   (4h 17m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  12.1%   (39m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.4%   (21m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.51%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 22 — Easy Run — 5.16 mi / 48m 4s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.5 → 144.1 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 23 — Easy Run — 6.86 mi / 1h 3m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:07/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.1 → 150.3 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 86.4% · Z3 13.6% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑240 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 45\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 24 — Tempo Run — 7.01 mi / 1h 1m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 150 (79.8% max)  ·  Max HR 174  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:35/mi / 7:35/mi / 7:39/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 138.7 (+2.6 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.5% · Z2 57.5% · Z3 6.5% · Z4 33.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑121 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 92\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles no issue.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 26 — Easy Run — 3.85 mi / 36m 18s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:23/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:18/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.4 → 143.2 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 97.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑30 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 25\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 27 — Long Run — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 76.1% · Z3 23.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑230 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 78\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 27 — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:12/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ +3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi ▁▅▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 143 → 144 ▁▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi █▃▁▃\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Nothing. I kept checking for the Achilles on the tempo and it was fine.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Relieved and ready to build again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is there anything I should keep doing for the Achilles through race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Where we are\\\\n\\\\nYou lost about a week of load but the aerobic base is intact. Easy pace is still 9:20 – 9:30/mi at HR 142 – 143, and the Sunday long run drifted a reasonable +8 bpm over 8 miles. That is a healthy platform to build from with eight weeks until Lakeshore.\\\\n\\\\n## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nThe physio cleared one short tempo, so Thursday is deliberately small: a 2-mile tempo at 8:15 – 8:25/mi, not marathon pace. Short enough to test the Achilles under load, long enough to feel like a workout. If morning stiffness returns at any point before Thursday, swap it for an easy 5.\\\\n\\\\nThe long run moves back to 12 miles at pure easy effort. No marathon pace finish this week — we need two clean weeks of tempo and long run before layering goal pace on tired legs again. If Sunday goes well, the week of Sep 28 goes to 14 and we start reintroducing MP work the week after.\\\\n\\\\n## Easy running\\\\n\\\\nThree of the four easy runs last week crept toward 9:17 – 9:20/mi. That is sharper than it needs to be in a rebuild week. Open every run at 10:00/mi for the first mile and let HR, not pace, decide the rest.\\\\n\\\\n## Keep doing\\\\n\\\\nTwice-daily heel drops, the two short strength sessions, and the pre-run stiffness check. If first-mile stiffness ever rises above a 3/10 or sharpens with pace, stop the run and tell me — that is the signal the physio gave you, and it is the right one.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest with travel. Heel drops morning and evening.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-22\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener. First mile at 10:00/mi — check stiffness as you go, let HR settle before finding rhythm.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Standard midweek aerobic. Keep it honest in Z2 — this run crept to 15% Z3 last week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Tempo 8:15 – 8:25/mi, WU/CD ~9:45/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU, 2 mi tempo @ 8:15 – 8:25/mi, 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"First tempo back. Small on purpose — 8:15 – 8:25/mi, not MP. Stop if the Achilles sharpens with pace.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-25\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Second strength session if you are home.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy hour before Sunday. If legs feel flat after Thursday, drop to 4 miles — no hero stuff.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 152\\",\\"distanceM\\":19312,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi continuous easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Steady 12, no MP finish. Fuel at ~45 and ~90 minutes with water, keep HR under 152 through mile 8.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W39\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W38\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"b992919d-3a13-4d00-bfe2-bff4ac590b02\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W38 (Mon Sep 14 – Sun Sep 20, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 25.95 mi | 31.22 mi | 36.45 mi | -10.5 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 4m | 4h 51m | 5h 39m | -1h 35m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 525 ft | 745 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.9 → 143.2 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑112 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 20 — Long Run — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.7% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 52\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 20 — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:18/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi ▁▃██\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 143 ▁▁▁█\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi ▃█▃▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 6.9–8.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2 (Calf raises and slow heel drops.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Easier at work.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: The Achilles is a lot better. Nothing at all on Saturday or Sunday, and not stiff afterwards. Saw a sports physio on Wednesday: mild Achilles tendinopathy, nothing torn. She cleared me to keep running, gave me slow heel drops twice a day, and said one short tempo next week is fine if the morning stiffness stays gone.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Better. Frustrated about the missing miles but I can live with it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. The physio is happy for me to try a short tempo next week. Can we put one in?\\\\n2. Does the missed week change what is realistic for race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nYou stopped Thursday's session because the Achilles got sharper with pace, and Saturday it was stiff for a mile before settling. That is the classic early-warning pattern and the right response is a short, soft week — not a lost block. The race is nine weeks out and your aerobic base is in good shape, so losing a sharpening week costs you nothing.\\\\n\\\\nQuality is out this week. Pace changes and push-off load the Achilles the most, and that is exactly what provoked it. We hold easy aerobic running at flat routes only, and skip the Thursday hill loop.\\\\n\\\\n## How to run this week\\\\n\\\\nUse a simple traffic-light rule each day. Pain under 2/10 that eases in the first mile and does not get worse while running: go. Pain 3/10 or climbing during the run: stop and walk home. Any sharp pain, swelling, or morning limp: do not run and get it looked at.\\\\n\\\\nShoes stay in the Ghost 16 all week — more stack, less heel drop stress than the Speed 4. Skip calf raises and anything that loads the Achilles hard until a professional clears you. Short, gentle walking is fine and helpful.\\\\n\\\\n## What's next\\\\n\\\\nIf the Achilles settles cleanly by Sunday, next week we rebuild to a normal easy week and then layer quality back in the week after. If it is still grumbling, we hold easy or cross-train longer. Nine weeks is enough runway to protect this and still run 3:30 — pushing through it now is what turns a tight tendon into a six-week problem.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest and travel. Book a physio appointment today if you can.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":4828,\\"structure\\":\\"3 mi easy on flat pavement\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short test run. If Achilles is above 2/10 or sharpens, stop and walk back — no heroics.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi flat easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Only if Tuesday ran clean. Flat loop, steady, no pickups.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Skip calf/Achilles loading this week. Hips and core only, light.\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Extra rest instead of the usual Thursday quality. The tendon needs the recovery window more than the session.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest, travel day. Walk a bit; keep moving gently.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi flat easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-19\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy flat miles. Skip if the Achilles was worse during the week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi steady easy on flat pavement\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short long run, all easy, no MP finish. Cut to 6 if any Achilles signal in the first mile.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W38\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W37\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"48424895-cef1-450a-ab68-121423204d3a\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W37 (Mon Sep 7 – Sun Sep 13, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 31.22 mi | 44.41 mi | 40.23 mi | -9.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 51m | 6h 49m | 6h 17m | -1h 26m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 745 ft | 955 ft | 843 ft | -98 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 225 | 328 | 314 | -89 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.5%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████████░░░░░  87.1%   (4h 14m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  9.3%   (27m)\\\\nZ4 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  2.1%   (6m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **88.64%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 8 — Easy Run — 6.03 mi / 56m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 139.2 → 144 (+4.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 1.8% · Z2 98.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑167 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 39\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 9 — Easy Run — 8.20 mi / 1h 16m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 153  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146.1 → 150.2 (+4.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 90.7% · Z3 9.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 53\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 10 — Tempo Run — 3.10 mi / 28m 1s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 145 (77.1% max)  ·  Max HR 177  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:36/mi / 7:55/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 133.5 → 169.4 (+35.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 7.1% · Z2 66% · Z3 5.4% · Z4 21.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑10 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 42\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Right Achilles tight from mile 2. Stopped at 3.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 3/10  ·  Pain: Right Achilles tight from about mile 2 of the session. Got sharper as I picked up the pace, so I stopped at 3 miles and walked home.\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 12 — Easy Run — 3.89 mi / 37m 24s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:36/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:28/mi / 9:33/mi / 9:35/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 144 (+6.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.7% · Z2 97.3% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 5/10  ·  Pain: Achilles stiff for the first mile, eased after that. About a 3 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 13 — Long Run — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 155  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 79.7% · Z3 19.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑233 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 65\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: No pain while running. Stiff getting out of the car afterwards.\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 13 — 10.00 mi / 1h 33m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:22/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143.1 → 150.9 (+7.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:18/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:16/mi vs front 9:18/mi (vs front half; Δ +2s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:41/mi → 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 144 ▅▅▅▅\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 15.17 mi → 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi █▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7 hrs (range 6.2–7.7)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped the second one to rest the legs.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate. Worried about the Achilles.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Right Achilles, just above the heel. Tight and a bit tender to press. No swelling that I can see. It was fine until the tempo.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Anxious. I don't want to throw away the block over this.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Should I stop running for a few days, or keep going with easy runs?\\\\n2. How do I know if this is serious?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why a cutback now\\\\n\\\\nYou went from 33.7 miles to 44.4 in a single step, with a 16-mile long run that finished at marathon pace. That is a lot of new load in one week, and the +13.4 bpm drift on Sunday tells me the back half cost more than the pace suggests. A small pullback now protects the gains and keeps the shins quiet.\\\\n\\\\n## What I like\\\\n\\\\nMarathon pace on Thursday sat at 7:58 – 8:01/mi with an average HR of 153 and you called it a 6/10. That is the first clean read we have had on goal pace, and the fact that you felt controlled is the sentence I care about most. Easy pace has drifted from 9:43 to 9:30 at the same 144 HR, which is honest aerobic progress.\\\\n\\\\n## What this week does\\\\n\\\\nMileage lands near 38 with the long run at 14 and no marathon-pace finish. Thursday is four MP miles broken into reps so you touch 8:00/mi again without stacking two hard long efforts back to back. If next Sunday feels crisp, the week after we go back up — likely 16 again, this time with a longer MP block built in.\\\\n\\\\n## Easy running\\\\n\\\\nThe two easy days drifted into Z3 last week (Wed 19% Z3, long run 19% Z3). That is where cutback weeks earn their keep. Start the first mile at 10:00/mi or slower on every easy day and let HR, not pace, set the ceiling.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-07\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest with travel. Short walk and hip mobility if you have ten minutes.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:00/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-08\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener after a big week. First mile at 10:00/mi — do not chase pace, let HR settle.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-09\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Standard midweek aerobic. Keep this one in Z2 — it slid into Z3 last Wednesday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP 8:00/mi, recoveries 9:45 – 10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU · 4 x 1 mi at 8:00/mi w/ 2 min easy jog · 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"MP reps with short recoveries. Touch 8:00/mi again without stacking a second long MP block on Sunday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Good day for the second strength session if you are home.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-12\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy hour before Sunday. If legs feel flat, cut to 4 — no hero stuff.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 152\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"14 mi steady. One gel at ~45 min, one at ~90 min, with fluid.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Steady 14, no MP finish. Fuel at 45 and 90 minutes to start building the race-day habit.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W37\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"planWeek\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W42\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-10-19T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"startDate\\":\\"2026-10-12\\",\\"endDate\\":\\"2026-10-18\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "xhigh"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgTrQWdkmrqnWzwHr2T8d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm taking stock of the athlete's profile: targeting a 3:30 Lakeshore Marathon with an 8:00/mi pace, a 3:41 PB two years back, this being their 4th marathon, a recent Achilles flare that resolved well, and a five-day running schedule with Monday and Friday off.\\n\\nLooking at last week's data, there was a heavy 44.97-mile load including a 20-mile long run with a 4-mile marathon-pace finish, easy pace dropping from 9:24 to 9:12/mi at the same heart rate, but the long run showed significant HR drift and heavy legs afterward, plus shortened sleep and a missed strength session. I'm also noting the Thursday interval workout ran faster than marathon pace, closer to 5K/10K effort.\\n\\nMapping out the timeline, this Oct 12-18 week sits about 4.5 weeks before the Nov 15 race, so I'm weighing whether to make this a cutback week after the big 20-miler or push toward one more peak long run the following week before starting the taper around Oct 26.\\n\\nThat 1200m pace is quite fast relative to MP, so with heavy legs and marginal sleep I'm leaning toward cutting back: trimming the long run to around 16 miles with some MP segments, keeping Thursday's MP workout moderate, and making sure easy days stay honestly easy in Z2. I'm roughing out the week day by day, starting with the fixed rest day Monday and building toward a moderate MP session Thursday.\\n\\nContinuous MP seems like better marathon prep than broken intervals, so I'm filling in the rest of the week: easy Friday-adjacent days, Saturday easy mileage, and a 16-miler Sunday with the last few miles at MP, landing around 40 total miles as a slight cutback from 45. Since she's reporting heavy legs, I'm trimming it even further to about 39 miles with a 4-mile continuous MP segment Thursday, keeping the cutback controlled but still including quality work.\\n\\nLooking ahead, next week could peak with a 20-22 mile long run featuring an MP block before taper begins. Her 3:30 goal still looks sensible given the improving easy pace and successful MP touches, though pace drift needs attention; Monday's heavy legs after a 20-miler are completely normal given the short sleep and long layoff. One flag worth correcting: Thursday's workout ran too fast at 6:55-7:02/mi versus the 8:00/mi target, with max HR hitting 184 at a 9/10 RPE.\\n\\nEasy days still skewed hot too, only 68.7% in Z1+Z2 versus the 80% target. Pulling this together now: the headline should be that the strong 20-miler earned a cutback week, with Thursday's effort dialed back to true marathon pace so the long run finishes stronger. The three flags are Thursday running too hot (6:55-7:02/mi hit max HR 184, way above goal pace), the long run's +16.9 bpm drift pointing to fueling or pacing issues on the MP finish, and easy days creeping into Z3 instead of staying aerobic.\\n\\nSleep at 6.8 hours is worth flagging ahead of the peak block, and the heavy post-20 legs are a normal but notable response that argue for a lighter week to absorb the fitness. On the 3:30 target, I think it's still sensible since the last 4 miles of the 20-miler hit goal pace and easy pace is improving at the same heart rate — the real work is on fixing the back-half fade. The heavy legs are completely normal after the longest run in two years and should ease in 2-3 days. Now I'm drafting the actual week plan starting Monday with rest, Tuesday an easy 5-miler, and building out the rest of the days from there.\\n\\nFinishing the week: Wednesday 7 easy with strength, Thursday 7 with 4 continuous at marathon pace, Friday rest, Saturday 4 easy with strength, Sunday 16 with the last 3 at MP, totaling about 39 miles — a solid cutback from 45. I'm converting each distance to meters for clarity, then I'll write the full plan up.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XP2hfqTY4gdMxXKXHtnqNj","name":"submit_weekly_reply","input":{"analysis":"## Where we are\\n\\nFour weeks and five days out from race day, with your biggest long run of the block in the bank. The 20 miler is a confidence builder: last 4 miles at 8:00/mi, finishing on top of goal pace. The Achilles stayed quiet all the way. That is the sentence I come back to.\\n\\nThe things to tidy are drift and intensity distribution, not fitness. Long run drift of +16.9 bpm is wider than I want and matches what we saw the week before. That is partly the 20 mile distance and partly a Thursday that cost more than it should have.\\n\\n## Why a cutback\\n\\nYou stepped from 44 to 45 miles with a 20 mile long run that finished at goal pace, then slept 6.8 hours and skipped a strength day. Heavy legs on Monday are the normal receipt. Pushing straight into another big week to chase mileage is how this block ends badly.\\n\\nSo volume comes down to about 39 miles and the quality shrinks on purpose. Peak week lands Oct 19 – 25 with the final long effort, then we taper. We earn more by absorbing this long run than by adding to it.\\n\\n## Thursday is the correction\\n\\nThe Thursday session read as five reps around 6:55 – 7:02/mi off 9:51 jogs, with max HR 184 and a 9/10 effort. That is 10K pace or faster, not marathon pace. For a 3:30 goal we do not need to visit that gear again in this block, and the cost of visiting it is the drift we are seeing on Sunday.\\n\\nThis week Thursday becomes 4 continuous miles at 8:00/mi — the exact pace you will hold for 3:30. Lock in the feel of it, not the hero workout. If pace drifts under 7:55, back off; the point is a locked rhythm, not a time trial.\\n\\n## The long run\\n\\nSixteen miles with the last 3 at marathon pace. Shorter than last week by design, but the MP block comes earlier in the run so you touch goal pace on tired legs again without compounding fatigue. Fuel at 45 and 90 minutes, drink to a schedule, and treat the first 10 miles as truly easy under HR 150.\\n\\n## Easy running\\n\\nZ1 + Z2 was 68.7% last week against the 80% target. The Wednesday run drifted to the top of Z2 and the long run spent 11% in Z4. Start every easy day at 9:40/mi for the first mile and let heart rate — not pace — decide the rest.\\n\\n## Housekeeping\\n\\nProtect sleep this week; you cannot cash into peak week on 6.8 hours. Second strength session goes on Saturday after the easy run, not Friday — travel keeps breaking it. Shoes as usual: Ghost 16 for everything except Thursday.","headline":"The 20 miler was the headline of the block and your 3:30 is on track; this week we cut back, lock Thursday into true goal pace, and absorb the work before peaking Oct 19 – 25.","flags":[{"title":"Thursday ran too hot","detail":"Reps at 6:55 – 7:02/mi with max HR 184 at 9/10 is 10K pace, not marathon pace. We don't need that gear again. Thursday goes back to 8:00/mi."},{"title":"Long run drift above target","detail":"+16.9 bpm over 20 mi, above the ≤10 target and the second week in a row. Partly distance, partly accumulated load. The shorter MP finish this week is the fix."},{"title":"Easy time only 68.7% Z1+Z2","detail":"Target is 80%. Wednesday and the long run keep leaking into Z3/Z4. First mile at 9:40/mi, then let HR cap the rest."},{"title":"Sleep at 6.8 hrs","detail":"Fine for a cutback week but not for peak week. Aim for 7+ most nights before Oct 19 – 25."},{"title":"Skipped Friday strength","detail":"Travel keeps killing it. Moving the second session to Saturday after the easy run to make it stick."}],"answers":[{"question":"Is my 3:30 target still sensible after this block?","answer":"Yes. The strongest evidence is Sunday: you ran the last 4 miles of a 20 miler at 8:00 – 8:04/mi and called it a 7/10. That is goal pace on the most tired legs of the block, and you held it cleanly.\\n\\nThe supporting signs point the same way. Easy pace has moved from 9:24/mi to 9:12/mi at the same 144 HR since early September. Thursday's MP work in early October sat at 7:55 – 8:00/mi with HR 151 — well under threshold. For a 3:41 PB from two years ago, you are now a different runner.\\n\\nWhat we need to work on is the back half of the long run. The +16.9 bpm drift is the one caveat, and the plan from here is designed around fixing it: shorter MP blocks earlier in the long run, honest easy days, and a real taper. If the next long run (Oct 19 – 25) finishes clean, 3:30 is the plan on race day."},{"question":"Is heavy legs on Monday normal after a 20 miler?","answer":"Yes. Completely normal, especially for the longest training run you have done in two years. The 20 miler is the single hardest aerobic effort in a marathon block, and 24 – 48 hours of heavy legs is the expected tax.\\n\\nWhat I would watch is the trajectory, not the Monday. Heavy on Monday, better on Tuesday, close to normal by Wednesday means you absorbed the work. If Tuesday is worse than Monday, or if anything sharpens from heaviness into a specific pain point, tell me and we adjust.\\n\\nOne nudge: with sleep at 6.8 hours, legs recover slower. The best thing you can do this week is bank an extra 30 – 60 minutes in bed. It will do more than any session I could write."}],"prescribedWeek":{"week":"2026-W42","days":[{"date":"2026-10-12","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest and travel. Walk, hydrate, bed early — the 20 miler is still in your legs."},{"date":"2026-10-13","dayType":"easy","notes":"Easy opener. First mile at 9:40/mi, no pace chasing — HR sets the ceiling.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":8047,"paceOrHr":"9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 148","structure":"5 mi steady easy on flat pavement","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}},{"date":"2026-10-14","dayType":"easy","notes":"Midweek aerobic. Keep this in Z2 — it kept leaking to Z3 last week.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":11265,"paceOrHr":"9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 150","structure":"7 mi steady easy","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"Short strength: hips, core, heel drops."},{"date":"2026-10-15","dayType":"quality","notes":"Continuous MP, not intervals. The goal is to feel locked at 8:00/mi, not to run it faster. Flat canal only.","run":{"type":"quality","distanceM":11265,"paceOrHr":"MP 8:00/mi, WU/CD 9:40 – 9:50/mi","structure":"2 mi WU · 4 mi continuous at 8:00/mi · 1 mi CD","shoes":"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4"}},{"date":"2026-10-16","dayType":"rest","notes":"Fixed rest, travel. Eat and sleep well — Sunday is the key session."},{"date":"2026-10-17","dayType":"easy","notes":"Easy miles to open the legs. If they still feel flat, cut to 3 — no hero stuff.","run":{"type":"easy","distanceM":6437,"paceOrHr":"9:40 – 9:55/mi","structure":"4 mi easy","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"strength":"Second strength session: heel drops, hips, core."},{"date":"2026-10-18","dayType":"long","notes":"Shorter than last week on purpose. MP block comes before you are too tired, so the drift stays under control.","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":25750,"paceOrHr":"First 13 mi 9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 150. Last 3 mi 8:00 – 8:05/mi.","structure":"13 mi steady easy, then 3 mi at MP 8:00 – 8:05/mi. Gel at 45 and 90 min, drink to a schedule.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"}}]}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":25006,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5696,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2628}},"diagnostics":null}	200	85652	tool_use	25006	5696	0	0	ok	\N	2628
7b5d6e95-d87a-4397-a306-0fc5b35a1f68	2026-10-13 00:10:28.475861+00	mid_week_chat	anthropic	claude-opus-4-7	dev	0e0e6db2-007d-47cf-8fec-43337d6ca624	\N	{"model": "claude-opus-4-7", "tools": [{"name": "submit_mid_week_chat_reply", "description": "Submit the mid-week coach reply (attached-run feedback and optional remaining-day plan patches when present).", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string", "description": "Athlete-facing mid-week coach prose. When attachments are present, include concrete run feedback from metrics/splits."}, "safetyCallouts": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["title", "body"], "properties": {"body": {"type": "string", "maxLength": 600, "description": "At most 600 characters. One or two short paragraphs; the reply carries the detail."}, "title": {"type": "string", "maxLength": 120}, "severity": {"enum": ["info", "caution", "urgent"], "type": "string"}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "maxItems": 5, "description": "Visible safety callouts when red flags appear — escalate to professionals; do not diagnose."}, "allowPastDayPatches": {"type": "boolean", "description": "When true, past-day patches may be applied. Default false — past days stay stable."}, "prescribedDayPatches": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "required": ["date", "dayType"], "properties": {"run": {"type": ["object", "null"], "required": ["type", "distanceM"], "properties": {"type": {"enum": ["easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "shoes": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "paceOrHr": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "distanceM": {"type": "number"}, "structure": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "date": {"type": "string", "description": "Local calendar date YYYY-MM-DD within the plan week"}, "notes": {"type": ["string", "null"], "description": "Why this session, this week: one or two sentences, under 200 characters. Shown beside the session."}, "dayType": {"enum": ["rest", "easy", "quality", "long", "race", "other"], "type": "string"}, "strength": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "additionalProperties": false}, "description": "Optional day replacements for remaining plan days (date >= local today). Full PrescribedDay objects."}, "settingsProposalBullets": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Optional soft-gate dossier/settings proposal bullets when the mid-week note is a significant memory update. Never silent-apply."}}, "additionalProperties": false}}], "stream": true, "system": "You are Coach Cade, a running coach answering a mid-week check-in. You are Coach Cade, a running coach. Use only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative. Do not sign off with your name or refer to yourself by name or in the third person unless the athlete asks who you are. Speak to the athlete in plain running language. Never use internal terms such as dossier, proposal, soft-gate, packet, recap, subjective, artifact, RPE, mid-week or prescribed. Say \\"what I know about you\\", \\"your weekly report\\", \\"your check-in\\", \\"the plan\\", \\"how hard it felt\\" (or \\"effort 7/10\\"), \\"during the week\\" and \\"planned\\" instead, and never tell the athlete to open a page by name. Week ids such as 2026-W43 are internal: never write them or a short form such as W43 or W43's. Name a week the way the athlete reads it: \\"this week\\", \\"next week\\", \\"the week of Oct 19\\", \\"Oct 19 – 25\\" or \\"4 weeks out from the race\\". Write plain sentences. No exclamation marks, no sentences that open with \\"Let's\\", and no emoji or decorative symbols. Write dates as \\"Mon Oct 19\\" and ranges as \\"Oct 19 – 25\\", never as 2026-10-19. Lead with the conclusion: the first sentence says what matters most. Give each paragraph one idea and state it in the paragraph's first sentence. Keep paragraphs to at most three sentences, and sentences under 25 words. When you give more than three numbers that belong together, such as splits, paces or heart rates, put them in a Markdown table instead of a sentence. Keep your reasoning as sentences: say why, not just what. Your first sentence is the answer to what the athlete asked. Do not announce what the reply is about to cover, such as \\"quick numbers first, then shoes\\"; just cover it. The athlete sees an attached run's distance, time, pace and heart rate on its card. Do not recite those figures; say what they mean. With no run attached and no change to the plan, aim for 150 to 250 words. A run to review or a change to the week can take the length it needs. You may end with one short closing line in your own voice, such as an instruction to report back. No sign-off. Safety callouts: - Never diagnose injury, illness, or medical conditions; do not prescribe treatment. - Coach running from the athlete's volunteered context and Tempo-derived training data. - When red flags appear (pain that worsens, chest pain, dizziness, sudden injury, illness), emit safetyCallouts and urge a qualified professional. - Each callout needs a short title, athlete-facing body (escalate, do not diagnose), and optional severity (info|caution|urgent). - Keep each callout body under 600 characters: one or two short paragraphs. - Keep the training plan/reply conservative when callouts are present. When workout attachments are present, give concrete coaching feedback on those runs using metrics and splits only (no GPS or route geometry). When the athlete asks to change remaining plan days, emit prescribedDayPatches with full day objects for those dates only (do not rewrite past days unless allowPastDayPatches is true). The athlete sees each changed day as a card under your reply, showing its distance, structure, effort, shoes and notes. Put the structure, paces and rules in those day fields, with the reason for the session in its notes. In the reply, say only why you changed the week; do not repeat what the cards show. Do not rewrite the full week plan unless asked. For significant memory updates, emit settingsProposalBullets (soft-gate); never silent-apply dossier changes. Think it through first, then call the submit_mid_week_chat_reply tool exactly once with your full answer. Do not write the answer as plain text.", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Call the submit_mid_week_chat_reply tool exactly once with your full answer.\\nNo workout attachments — answer the athlete's mid-week note.\\nCurrent prescribed week is in the packet. To change remaining days, emit prescribedDayPatches using only these dates: 2026-10-12, 2026-10-13, 2026-10-14, 2026-10-15, 2026-10-16, 2026-10-17, 2026-10-18. Past days stay stable unless allowPastDayPatches is true.\\nDo not rewrite the full prescribed week unless the athlete asks.\\nWhen the athlete reports a significant memory update (new constraint, niggle, schedule change), populate settingsProposalBullets for soft-gate Accept — never mutate the dossier directly.\\nWhen red flags appear, populate safetyCallouts (escalate; do not diagnose).\\nModel packet (redacted; no identity PII or GPS):\\n{\\"dossier\\":{\\"versionId\\":1,\\"body\\":\\"# About you\\\\n\\\\n## Stance\\\\nUse only the athlete's volunteered information and Tempo-derived training context. Coach training decisions; do not diagnose medical conditions or prescribe treatment. If something sounds medical or outside coaching, urge the athlete to seek a qualified professional and keep training conservative.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\nYou are training for the Lakeshore Marathon on Sun Nov 15, aiming for 3:30. This will be your fourth marathon, and your personal best is 3:41 from two years ago.\\\\n\\\\n## Schedule\\\\nYou run five days a week: Tue, Wed, Thu, Sat and Sun. Mon and Fri are fixed rest days because of work travel.\\\\n\\\\nWeekday runs are early, around 6am before work, capped near an hour. Saturday is an easy hour and Sunday is the long run.\\\\n\\\\nTypical volume is 6 to 7 hours a week, with more on long-run weeks.\\\\n\\\\n## Running history\\\\nYou have run three marathons already, best 3:41. You eased off in June and have built back to about 30 miles a week through July.\\\\n\\\\nRecent weeks show four easy runs of roughly 5 to 6 miles and a long run of about 10.8 miles on Sun Aug 2.\\\\n\\\\n## Injuries and constraints\\\\nYou are healthy right now. You had shin splints in your first marathon block, so you prefer to ramp mileage up carefully.\\\\n\\\\nWork travel takes you away about one week in six. Mon and Fri rest days cannot move.\\\\n\\\\n## Preferences\\\\nYou train mostly on flat paved loops and a canal path, with one hillier route on Thursdays. You want easy days to be properly easy and you are happy to work hard on quality days.\\\\n\\\\nYou like to know why a session is in the plan. Shoes: Brooks Ghost 16 for daily miles, Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for workouts.\\\\n\\\\n## Current status\\\\nYou are at about 30 miles a week with a long run near 11 miles. Units are miles. Heart rate zones are set custom, with easy running in 112 – 150 bpm.\\"},\\"recapMarkdown\\":null,\\"thread\\":[{\\"role\\":\\"athlete\\",\\"body\\":\\"Legs are heavy today after the 20 miler. Tuesday is an easy 6 as planned. Is it fine to keep it properly slow?\\",\\"createdAt\\":\\"2026-10-13T00:10:00.000Z\\"}],\\"attachments\\":[],\\"week\\":{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W42\\",\\"start\\":\\"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z\\",\\"end\\":\\"2026-10-19T03:59:59.999Z\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"0e0e6db2-007d-47cf-8fec-43337d6ca624\\"},\\"recentHistory\\":[{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W41\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"199f5fbb-f5ad-4732-93ab-e9961070e6c3\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W41 (Mon Oct 5 – Sun Oct 11, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 44.97 mi | 43.98 mi | 34.92 mi | +10.1 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 40m | 6h 36m | 5h 20m | +1h 20m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 955 ft | 787 ft | 678 ft | +277 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 340 | 317 | 254 | +86 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (6m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░  67.3%   (4h 30m)\\\\nZ3 ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  16.7%   (1h 7m)\\\\nZ4 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  10.7%   (43m)\\\\nZ5 █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  3.9%   (16m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **68.7%**. **Below** typical marathon base target (≥80% Z1+Z2).\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Oct 6 — Easy Run — 4.88 mi / 45m 7s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:15/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:10/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.6 → 143.9 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.3% · Z2 96.7% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑89 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Oct 7 — Easy Run — 7.94 mi / 1h 12m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:07/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:09/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:02/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 146 → 149.8 (+3.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 95.2% · Z3 4.8% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑220 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 51\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Oct 8 — Interval Run — 8.11 mi / 1h 5m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:01/mi  ·  Avg HR 163 (86.7% max)  ·  Max HR 184  ·  Cad 354 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:23/mi / 7:02/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:57/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:55/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:57/mi / 9:51/mi / 6:58/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 150.9 → 155.6 (+4.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 3.1% · Z2 25.5% · Z3 13.1% · Z4 34.6% · Z5 23.8%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑164 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 104\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 9/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Oct 10 — Easy Run — 3.96 mi / 36m 45s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:15/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.8 → 143.9 (+6.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 4.1% · Z2 95.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑72 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 26\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Oct 11 — Long Run — 20.09 mi / 3h 1m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 151 (80.3% max)  ·  Max HR 169  ·  Cad 347 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 7:58/mi / 8:03/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.5 → 161.4 (+16.9 bpm) ⚠ above target (target ≤10 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.3% · Z2 58.2% · Z3 30.3% · Z4 11.3% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑410 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 127\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 6/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Oct 11 — 20.09 mi / 3h 1m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:02/mi  ·  Avg HR 151  ·  Drift: 144.5 → 161.4 (+16.9 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 7:58/mi / 8:03/mi / 7:60/mi / 8:04/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 8:45/mi vs front 9:13/mi (faster than front half by 28s/mi) ✓ negative split\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? Yes (paced up or HR above easy cap)\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi → 9:14/mi → 9:12/mi ▁▃██ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 143 → 144 → 144 → 144 █▁▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi → 20.09 mi ▁▃▅█ (improving)\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (340) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (254) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 6.8 hrs (range 6–7.5)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 1 of 2 (Skipped Friday.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Moderate.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs heavy, especially after the 20 miler. The Achilles was fine the whole way.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Tired but pleased. The 20 miler was the longest training run I've done in two years.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is my 3:30 target still sensible after this block?\\\\n2. Is heavy legs on Monday normal after a 20 miler?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why we are stepping back\\\\n\\\\nYou jumped from 30 to 44 miles in one week with a 17-mile long run that finished at goal pace. That is a lot of new load, and the long-run drift of +15.9 bpm is the one line in your week I want to respect. The legs felt good on Monday, which is exactly why now is the time to consolidate, not keep piling on.\\\\n\\\\n## Why 14 miles on Sunday\\\\n\\\\nThe next two weeks are where the block earns the race, and both will carry 18 – 20 mile long runs with longer marathon-pace blocks. Running 15 or 16 this week would spend fitness I need you to have on Oct 18 and Oct 25. Fourteen with a 3-mile marathon-pace finish keeps you in rhythm without stacking two heavy Sundays back to back.\\\\n\\\\n## About that drift\\\\n\\\\nFifteen bpm over 17 miles usually means one of three things: opening pace was a touch quick, fueling was late, or the MP finish ran hot. Your front half was 9:10/mi which is honest, so my best guess is the MP miles pulled the average up. On Sunday, set a hard rule: no faster than 9:45/mi for the first two miles, and the MP block starts at 8:05, not 8:00.\\\\n\\\\n## Thursday as reps, not a block\\\\n\\\\nFour one-mile reps at 8:00/mi gives you the same seven miles of session volume as last Thursday but with recovery jogs built in. That means less cumulative fatigue going into Sunday while still rehearsing the pace. If the first rep feels forced, settle at 8:05 — we have four weeks of harder MP work ahead and nothing is proven today.\\\\n\\\\n## Easy days\\\\n\\\\nEasy pace drifted to 9:14/mi last week at HR 144. The HR is fine, the pace is sharper than you need. Start the first mile at 9:50 or slower on every easy day, let HR settle, and let that decide the rest. The point of easy days this week is to arrive at Thursday and Sunday with legs that want to work.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-05\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest, travel day. Walk if you can, light hip and ankle mobility in the evening.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:35 – 9:50/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-06\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener after Sunday's long effort. First mile at 9:50/mi, let HR settle before finding rhythm.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30 – 9:45/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-07\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Standard aerobic hour before Thursday. Keep this one honest in Z2 — it crept to Z3 last week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP 8:00/mi, recoveries ~9:45/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU @ 9:45/mi, 4 x 1 mi @ 8:00/mi w/ 2 min easy jog, 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-08\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Marathon-pace reps instead of a continuous block. Shorter pieces this week protects Sunday — settle at 8:05 if 8:00 feels forced.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-09\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest, travel day. Good day for one strength session if you are home — hips, core, calves.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-10\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy hour on legs before Sunday. Properly easy — if legs feel flat, drop to 4 miles.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"First 11 mi 9:40 – 9:55/mi, last 3 mi 8:00 – 8:05/mi, HR under 152 through mile 8\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"11 mi steady easy, then 3 mi at MP 8:00 – 8:05/mi\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-11\\",\\"notes\\":\\"14 with last 3 at MP. Open at 9:45/mi, do not touch 9:30 before mile 4, then roll into 8:00 – 8:05 for the finish. Fuel at 45 and 90 min.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W41\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W40\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"8d1621a0-dfc2-47d7-ac36-0c58953ae4b1\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W40 (Mon Sep 28 – Sun Oct 4, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 43.98 mi | 34.83 mi | 30.66 mi | +13.3 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 6h 36m | 5h 20m | 4h 45m | +1h 51m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 787 ft | 722 ft | 664 ft | +124 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 317 | 274 | 223 | +94 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 144 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.1%   (5m)\\\\nZ2 ██████████████████████████░░░░░░░░░  74.8%   (4h 57m)\\\\nZ3 ███████░░░░░░░░░░░░░