\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi → 9:14/mi ▁▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 143 → 144 → 144 ▁█▁▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi → 17.18 mi ▃▁▃█\\\\n\\\\n## Notable\\\\n\\\\n- Relative effort (317) ≥ 1.3× 3-wk avg (223) — possible overload\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 7–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Legs tired after the long run but nothing sore. Achilles quiet.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Good. The last three miles at marathon pace were hard but I could have held it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. How should the final weeks before the race look?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nLast week was the first full load since the Achilles flare and it held together: tempo at 7:35/mi, long run at 9:18/mi with only +8.8 bpm drift, and no body-check flags. That earns a careful step up, not a leap. Seven weeks to race day means two more build weeks, then a peak block, then taper.\\\\n\\\\n## The quality day\\\\n\\\\nThursday is 2 x 2 miles at marathon pace with a 3-minute jog between. That is a longer continuous touch of 8:00/mi than the three Thursday tempo miles you ran last week, but still well short of the 8-mile MP session from early September. Stay on the flat canal loop, not the Thursday hills — pace changes and climbs are what loaded the tendon last time.\\\\n\\\\n## The long run\\\\n\\\\nFourteen miles Sunday with the last 2 at marathon pace. This is the first MP-on-tired-legs rep since the Achilles episode, kept deliberately short so you finish wanting more. If anything whispers in the tendon during the first 10 miles, drop the MP finish and jog it home — no points for toughing it out this far from the race.\\\\n\\\\n## Guardrails\\\\n\\\\nKeep the heel drops going daily, keep the Ghost 16 for everything except Thursday, and keep easy days honest (HR under 150). Wednesday drifted to 13.6% Z3 last week — fine, but let's keep it Z2 this week with Thursday getting harder.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-28\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest and travel. Heel drops morning and evening.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy on flat pavement\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-29\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener. First mile deliberately slow to let the tendon warm through.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:25 – 9:45/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-30\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Midweek aerobic. Keep this in Z2 — it drifted to Z3 last week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Short strength: hips, core, slow heel drops.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"MP 8:00/mi, recoveries 9:45/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":12070,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU · 2 x 2 mi at 8:00/mi w/ 3 min easy jog · 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-01\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Longer MP touch than last week, still short of September's tempo. Flat canal only — no hills.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-02\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest, travel. Walk, eat, sleep well for Sunday.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30 – 9:50/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-03\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short easy hour on legs to set up Sunday. Properly easy.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Second strength session: heel drops, hips, core.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"First 12 mi 9:30 – 9:50/mi, last 2 mi 8:00 – 8:05/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":22531,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi steady easy, then 2 mi at MP 8:00 – 8:05/mi\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-04\\",\\"notes\\":\\"14 mi with a short MP finish — first MP-on-tired-legs since the Achilles. Drop the MP if anything whispers in the first 10.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W40\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W39\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"2453cc65-d713-4a3d-b143-23203b4e72e5\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W39 (Mon Sep 21 – Sun Sep 27, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 34.83 mi | 25.95 mi | 33.86 mi | +1.0 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 5h 20m | 4h 4m | 5h 15m | +5m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 722 ft | 525 ft | 741 ft | -20 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 274 | 171 | 241 | +33 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 144 | 143 | 144 | +0 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.2%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ████████████████████████████░░░░░░░  80.3%   (4h 17m)\\\\nZ3 ████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  12.1%   (39m)\\\\nZ4 ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  6.4%   (21m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **81.51%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 22 — Easy Run — 5.16 mi / 48m 4s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:17/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.5 → 144.1 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑102 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 34\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 23 — Easy Run — 6.86 mi / 1h 3m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:17/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:07/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:15/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 145.1 → 150.3 (+5.2 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 86.4% · Z3 13.6% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑240 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 45\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 24 — Tempo Run — 7.01 mi / 1h 1m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 8:43/mi  ·  Avg HR 150 (79.8% max)  ·  Max HR 174  ·  Cad 350 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 7:35/mi / 7:35/mi / 7:39/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:31/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 136.1 → 138.7 (+2.6 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.5% · Z2 57.5% · Z3 6.5% · Z4 33.5% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑121 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 92\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles no issue.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 7/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 26 — Easy Run — 3.85 mi / 36m 18s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 147  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:23/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:30/mi / 9:18/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.4 → 143.2 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.8% · Z2 97.2% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑30 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 25\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 27 — Long Run — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 156  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.5% · Z2 76.1% · Z3 23.5% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑230 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 78\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 5/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 27 — 11.94 mi / 1h 51m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:18/mi  ·  Avg HR 148  ·  Drift: 142.7 → 151.6 (+8.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:07/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:12/mi / 9:04/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:12/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ +3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi → 9:20/mi ▁▅▅█\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 143 → 144 ▁▁█▁\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi → 11.94 mi █▃▁▃\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.4 hrs (range 6.8–8)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: Nothing. I kept checking for the Achilles on the tempo and it was fine.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Relieved and ready to build again.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. Is there anything I should keep doing for the Achilles through race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Where we are\\\\n\\\\nYou lost about a week of load but the aerobic base is intact. Easy pace is still 9:20 – 9:30/mi at HR 142 – 143, and the Sunday long run drifted a reasonable +8 bpm over 8 miles. That is a healthy platform to build from with eight weeks until Lakeshore.\\\\n\\\\n## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nThe physio cleared one short tempo, so Thursday is deliberately small: a 2-mile tempo at 8:15 – 8:25/mi, not marathon pace. Short enough to test the Achilles under load, long enough to feel like a workout. If morning stiffness returns at any point before Thursday, swap it for an easy 5.\\\\n\\\\nThe long run moves back to 12 miles at pure easy effort. No marathon pace finish this week — we need two clean weeks of tempo and long run before layering goal pace on tired legs again. If Sunday goes well, the week of Sep 28 goes to 14 and we start reintroducing MP work the week after.\\\\n\\\\n## Easy running\\\\n\\\\nThree of the four easy runs last week crept toward 9:17 – 9:20/mi. That is sharper than it needs to be in a rebuild week. Open every run at 10:00/mi for the first mile and let HR, not pace, decide the rest.\\\\n\\\\n## Keep doing\\\\n\\\\nTwice-daily heel drops, the two short strength sessions, and the pre-run stiffness check. If first-mile stiffness ever rises above a 3/10 or sharpens with pace, stop the run and tell me — that is the signal the physio gave you, and it is the right one.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-21\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest with travel. Heel drops morning and evening.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-22\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener. First mile at 10:00/mi — check stiffness as you go, let HR settle before finding rhythm.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:45 – 10:00/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":9656,\\"structure\\":\\"6 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-23\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Standard midweek aerobic. Keep it honest in Z2 — this run crept to 15% Z3 last week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"quality\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Saucony Endorphin Speed 4\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"Tempo 8:15 – 8:25/mi, WU/CD ~9:45/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"2 mi WU, 2 mi tempo @ 8:15 – 8:25/mi, 1 mi CD\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-24\\",\\"notes\\":\\"First tempo back. Small on purpose — 8:15 – 8:25/mi, not MP. Stop if the Achilles sharpens with pace.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"quality\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-25\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest. Second strength session if you are home.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:00/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-26\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy hour before Sunday. If legs feel flat after Thursday, drop to 4 miles — no hero stuff.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 152\\",\\"distanceM\\":19312,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi continuous easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-27\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Steady 12, no MP finish. Fuel at ~45 and ~90 minutes with water, keep HR under 152 through mile 8.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W39\\"}},{\\"isoWeek\\":\\"2026-W38\\",\\"weekSessionId\\":\\"b992919d-3a13-4d00-bfe2-bff4ac590b02\\",\\"recapMarkdown\\":\\"# Weekly Recap — 2026-W38 (Mon Sep 14 – Sun Sep 20, 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Metric | This week | Prev week | 3-wk avg | Δ |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| Mileage | 25.95 mi | 31.22 mi | 36.45 mi | -10.5 |\\\\n| Runs | 5 | 5 | 5.0 | +0.0 |\\\\n| Total time | 4h 4m | 4h 51m | 5h 39m | -1h 35m |\\\\n| Total elevation | 525 ft | 745 ft | 762 ft | -237 ft |\\\\n| Relative effort | 171 | 225 | 275 | -104 |\\\\n| Avg easy-run HR | 143 | 144 | 144 | -1 |\\\\n\\\\n## HR zone distribution (week total)\\\\n\\\\nZ1 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  1.4%   (4m)\\\\nZ2 ███████████████████████████████░░░░  89.7%   (3h 39m)\\\\nZ3 ███░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  8.8%   (22m)\\\\nZ4 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\nZ5 ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  0%   (0m)\\\\n\\\\nTarget for marathon base phase: **≥80% in Z1+Z2**. This week: **91.18%**. On target for ≥80% Z1+Z2.\\\\n\\\\n## Run-by-run\\\\n\\\\n### Tue Sep 15 — Easy Run — 4.13 mi / 38m 32s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:22/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:12/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138.7 → 144.2 (+5.5 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑82 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 6/10  ·  Pain: Slight tightness for the first half mile, about a 2 out of 10.\\\\n\\\\n### Wed Sep 16 — Easy Run — 4.83 mi / 45m 6s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:20/mi  ·  Avg HR 148 (78.7% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:12/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 144.8 → 150.6 (+5.8 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0% · Z2 84.3% · Z3 15.7% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 32\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10  ·  Pain: A hint of it at the start only.\\\\n\\\\n### Thu Sep 17 — Easy Run — 4.99 mi / 46m 53s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:23/mi  ·  Avg HR 142 (75.5% max)  ·  Max HR 148  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:25/mi / 9:26/mi / 9:18/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:17/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 138 → 143.7 (+5.7 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.1% · Z2 97.9% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑135 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 33\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nNotes (from app): \\\\\\"Achilles fine on the flat. Easy only this week.\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 7/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sat Sep 19 — Easy Run — 4.07 mi / 38m 48s\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:31/mi  ·  Avg HR 141 (75% max)  ·  Max HR 146  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:26/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:22/mi / 9:28/mi / 9:30/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 137.9 → 143.2 (+5.3 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 2.6% · Z2 97.4% · Z3 0% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑112 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 27\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 3/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Sun Sep 20 — Long Run — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nPace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147 (78.2% max)  ·  Max HR 154  ·  Cad 344 spm\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nHR drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nTime in zones: Z1 0.7% · Z2 80.1% · Z3 19.3% · Z4 0% · Z5 0%\\\\n\\\\nElevation: ↑98 ft\\\\n\\\\nShoe: Brooks Ghost 16\\\\n\\\\nRelative effort: 52\\\\n\\\\nSimilar route: n/a\\\\n\\\\nRPE: 4/10  ·  Felt: 8/10\\\\n\\\\n### Long run — Sun Sep 20 — 7.93 mi / 1h 14m\\\\n\\\\nAvg pace: 9:26/mi  ·  Avg HR 147  ·  Drift: 143 → 151.1 (+8.1 bpm)\\\\n\\\\nSplits: 9:10/mi / 9:14/mi / 9:20/mi / 9:15/mi / 9:23/mi / 9:10/mi / 9:17/mi / 9:22/mi\\\\n\\\\nBack half avg pace: 9:18/mi vs front 9:15/mi (vs front half; Δ -3s/mi)\\\\n\\\\nLast 3 mi at marathon-pace effort? No\\\\n\\\\n## Trends\\\\n\\\\n- **Easy pace (≤Z2, list/detail approx.)**: 9:34/mi → 9:30/mi → 9:23/mi → 9:24/mi ▁▃██\\\\n\\\\n- **Avg easy HR**: 144 → 144 → 144 → 143 ▁▁▁█\\\\n\\\\n- **Long-run distance** (max long-typed, else max run in week): 10.86 mi → 16.10 mi → 10.00 mi → 7.93 mi ▃█▃▁\\\\n\\\\n## Subjective recap\\\\n\\\\nSleep avg this week: 7.5 hrs (range 6.9–8.2)\\\\n\\\\nStrength sessions completed: 2 of 2 (Calf raises and slow heel drops.)\\\\n\\\\nStress level: Low. Easier at work.\\\\n\\\\nBody check: The Achilles is a lot better. Nothing at all on Saturday or Sunday, and not stiff afterwards. Saw a sports physio on Wednesday: mild Achilles tendinopathy, nothing torn. She cleared me to keep running, gave me slow heel drops twice a day, and said one short tempo next week is fine if the morning stiffness stays gone.\\\\n\\\\nGoing into next week feeling: Better. Frustrated about the missing miles but I can live with it.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions for coach\\\\n\\\\n1. The physio is happy for me to try a short tempo next week. Can we put one in?\\\\n2. Does the missed week change what is realistic for race day?\\\\n\\",\\"analysis\\":\\"## Why this shape\\\\n\\\\nYou stopped Thursday's session because the Achilles got sharper with pace, and Saturday it was stiff for a mile before settling. That is the classic early-warning pattern and the right response is a short, soft week — not a lost block. The race is nine weeks out and your aerobic base is in good shape, so losing a sharpening week costs you nothing.\\\\n\\\\nQuality is out this week. Pace changes and push-off load the Achilles the most, and that is exactly what provoked it. We hold easy aerobic running at flat routes only, and skip the Thursday hill loop.\\\\n\\\\n## How to run this week\\\\n\\\\nUse a simple traffic-light rule each day. Pain under 2/10 that eases in the first mile and does not get worse while running: go. Pain 3/10 or climbing during the run: stop and walk home. Any sharp pain, swelling, or morning limp: do not run and get it looked at.\\\\n\\\\nShoes stay in the Ghost 16 all week — more stack, less heel drop stress than the Speed 4. Skip calf raises and anything that loads the Achilles hard until a professional clears you. Short, gentle walking is fine and helpful.\\\\n\\\\n## What's next\\\\n\\\\nIf the Achilles settles cleanly by Sunday, next week we rebuild to a normal easy week and then layer quality back in the week after. If it is still grumbling, we hold easy or cross-train longer. Nine weeks is enough runway to protect this and still run 3:30 — pushing through it now is what turns a tight tendon into a six-week problem.\\",\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest and travel. Book a physio appointment today if you can.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":4828,\\"structure\\":\\"3 mi easy on flat pavement\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short test run. If Achilles is above 2/10 or sharpens, stop and walk back — no heroics.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi flat easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Only if Tuesday ran clean. Flat loop, steady, no pickups.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Skip calf/Achilles loading this week. Hips and core only, light.\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Extra rest instead of the usual Thursday quality. The tendon needs the recovery window more than the session.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest, travel day. Walk a bit; keep moving gently.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi flat easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-19\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy flat miles. Skip if the Achilles was worse during the week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:50 – 10:10/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":12875,\\"structure\\":\\"8 mi steady easy on flat pavement\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-09-20\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short long run, all easy, no MP finish. Cut to 6 if any Achilles signal in the first mile.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W38\\"}}],\\"recentHistoryLimit\\":4,\\"prescribedWeek\\":{\\"days\\":[{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-12\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest and travel. Walk, hydrate, bed early — the 20 miler is still in your legs.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":8047,\\"structure\\":\\"5 mi steady easy on flat pavement\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-13\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy opener. First mile at 9:40/mi, no pace chasing — HR sets the ceiling.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 150\\",\\"distanceM\\":11265,\\"structure\\":\\"7 mi steady easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-14\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Midweek aerobic. Keep this in Z2 — it kept leaking to Z3 last week.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Short strength: hips, core, heel drops.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi, HR under 148\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi steady easy on flat pavement\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-15\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Short easy to fit the 40-minute window. The MP touch moves to Sunday — this one is just rhythm.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\"},{\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-16\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Fixed rest, travel. Eat and sleep well — Sunday is the key session.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"rest\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"easy\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"9:40 – 9:55/mi\\",\\"distanceM\\":6437,\\"structure\\":\\"4 mi easy\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-17\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Easy miles to open the legs. If they still feel flat, cut to 3 — no hero stuff.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"easy\\",\\"strength\\":\\"Second strength session: heel drops, hips, core.\\"},{\\"run\\":{\\"type\\":\\"long\\",\\"shoes\\":\\"Brooks Ghost 16\\",\\"paceOrHr\\":\\"First 12 mi 9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 150. Last 4 mi 8:00 – 8:05/mi.\\",\\"distanceM\\":25750,\\"structure\\":\\"12 mi steady easy, then 4 mi at MP 8:00 – 8:05/mi. Gel at 45 and 90 min, drink to a schedule.\\"},\\"date\\":\\"2026-10-18\\",\\"notes\\":\\"One more MP mile than planned to carry a bit of Thursday's work. Cap the MP at four — do not chase a fifth.\\",\\"dayType\\":\\"long\\"}],\\"week\\":\\"2026-W42\\"}}"}], "thinking": {"type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized"}, "max_tokens": 64000, "tool_choice": {"type": "auto"}, "output_config": {"effort": "xhigh"}}	{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CgTreaX4JfoiiB1cJyVtf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm looking at the medium-long run data and noting the Achilles discomfort around mile 7 that settled afterward — given the September tendinopathy history, this needs a clear safety flag before I address their shoe rotation plan for the block.\\n\\nSplits show the run was paced around 9:05/mi against a prescribed 9:30-9:50 window, with HR drifting gently from 147 to 153, staying mostly in Z2 but faster than intended. On the shoe front, switching all long runs and MP work to the Endorphin Speed 4 is a meaningful change worth flagging, since it's a carbon-plated speed shoe with a stack/drop profile that warrants caution given the Achilles history.\\n\\nI'm leaning toward acknowledging the athlete's preference, proposing the settings update, and suggesting a gradual transition where daily miles stay in the Ghost while watching for any Achilles signal during the first few long runs in the new shoe. For the schedule, Thursday's easy run doesn't need any change, but Sunday's long run — currently prescribed in the Ghost — should be updated to the Endorphin Speed 4 since the athlete specifically asked for long runs and MP work in that shoe going forward.\\n\\nGiven the Achilles whisper on today's run though, I think caution wins here: I'll keep Sunday's long run in the Ghost and plan to revisit the switch to Endorphin Speed next week if the Achilles stays clean. I want to lead with the safety callout around the Achilles and suggest a physio check-in before addressing the shoe change itself.\\n\\nKeep MP at four miles but drop it if there's any morning stiffness or Achilles whisper in the first 10 miles. The athlete's own question invites adjustment, so I'll update Sunday's note to keep the Ghost 16 (not switching shoes yet) and add an explicit caution flag about the Achilles signal rather than rewriting the whole week.\\n\\nFor the settings, I'll note the athlete's preference for Endorphin Speed 4 on long runs and MP work going forward, contingent on the Achilles staying calm. I'll add a safety callout referencing the September flare-up, suggesting a physio check-in before Sunday's MP block without diagnosing anything -- just flagging morning stiffness, pace-related sharpening, or pain lasting past the first mile. I'll write this in the coach's normal voice, and it's fine for the response to run a bit longer given the run review, Achilles concern, and shoe discussion all need covering.\\n\\nFor the structure, I'm leading with a note that today was aerobically clean but the Achilles comment plus the shoe plan need careful handling. Then I'll cover the run itself — pace crept to 9:05/mile versus the 9:30-9:50 target, though HR held steady at 148 with only +6 bpm drift, so it stayed Z2 effort overall; the back half quietly picked up speed with splits dropping under 9:00 by mile 8, which likely explains what the Achilles felt around mile 7. Then into the Achilles section — since this is the same tendon that flared in September, I'm recommending a physio touch-base before Sunday's MP session.\\n\\nOn the shoe plan, I want to keep Sunday in the Ghost 16 rather than switching to the Endorphin Speed 4 given today's signal, rolling the new shoe in for the long run on Oct 25 if things stay quiet. For Sunday itself, I'm keeping the structure but tightening the Achilles rule — drop the MP and jog home if anything flares in the first 10 miles. Closing with a request to check back after Thursday and after the physio visit, while also making sure each sentence stays under 25 words.\\n\\nI only need to patch Sunday Oct 18's long run, leaving Thursday and earlier days untouched, with the proposed settings noting the Endorphin Speed 4 for long runs/MP work going forward (pending the Achilles staying calm) and a safety callout to touch base with the physio.\\n\\nThe callout flags that today's Achilles flare-up is the same tendon from September, so a check-in before Sunday's MP block is wise, and I should watch for stiffness past the first mile, sharpening pain, or discomfort above 2/10 that worsens — any of which means dropping the MP finish from Sunday's run. Since this is a run review with a plan change, I can let the length run as needed, just avoiding overly clinical phrasing.\\n\\nI should suggest messaging the physio before Sunday as a precaution, even though the mid-run settle was reassuring. For shoes, Sunday stays in the Ghost 16 given today's twinge, with the Endorphin Speed 4 reserved for the long run on Oct 25–26 if the Achilles stays quiet. I'll keep Sunday's structure and the four MP miles intact, but add a rule to drop the MP finish and jog it in if anything flares in the first 10 miles.\\n\\nShortening that one down, I'm checking each remaining sentence for length — the pace and HR lines both land around 22 words, and the Achilles/physio sentences come in tighter at 12-18 words, so the rhythm reads fine across the paragraph.\\n\\nFor the shoe plan I need to split the run-on into two shorter pieces: keeping this Sunday in the Ghost 16 for cushioning since the tendon's still fresh, with the Speed 4 held back until next week's long run if things stay quiet.\\n\\nI'm also adding a rule to bail on the MP finish if anything flares in the first ten miles, and asking for an update after the physio visit plus how tomorrow's opener feels — double-checking that tomorrow lines up correctly with the easy run after today. Now I'm scanning the draft for any forbidden terms, confirming \\"mid-run\\" is fine since only \\"mid-week\\" was actually restricted.\\n\\nI'm double-checking the wording further—no exclamation marks, no \\"Let's,\\" no emojis, and I avoid the word \\"prescribed\\" in favor of phrasing like \\"tightened Sunday's note\\" with a 9:30–9:50 target. I'm also referencing the Oct 25–26 long run weekend as the next checkpoint, and sketching a short bullet list of settings to confirm with the athlete, starting with shoe choice.\\n\\nWriting the patch JSON...\\n\\nDrafting the safety callout now, keeping it escalation-focused on the Achilles flare-up and tying it to the September history, with clear triggers for pulling the MP finish. Checking length is under 600 characters and making sure there's no overlap with the body text or any sign-off.\\n\\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TqFhzosjetTrRYmN8jHk89","name":"submit_mid_week_chat_reply","input":{"allowPastDayPatches":false,"body":"Today was aerobically clean, but the Achilles note and the Endorphin Speed plan both deserve a careful answer before Sunday.\\n\\nThe pace crept sharper than I asked for — the back half ran well under 9:00/mi against a 9:30 – 9:50 target. HR stayed honest at 148 with gentle drift, so the engine was in Z2, but the legs were running Z3 pace. That quiet speed-up by mile 8 is probably what the Achilles noticed around mile 7.\\n\\nThe same tendon flared in September, so I am not going to brush past this. Please message your physio before Sunday's long run, even just a check-in. The mid-run settle is a good sign, not a green light to carry on as if nothing happened.\\n\\nOn shoes, happy to move long runs and MP work into the Endorphin Speed 4 for the rest of the block. Not this Sunday though. With today's whisper fresh, Sunday stays in the Ghost 16 — more cushion, less demand on the tendon. If the Achilles stays quiet through the week, the Speed 4 comes in on the long run of Oct 25 – 26.\\n\\nI have tightened Sunday's note with the Achilles rule — the structure and the four MP miles are unchanged. If anything whispers in the first 10 miles, drop the MP finish and jog it home.\\n\\nReport back after you have heard from the physio, and tell me how the opener feels tomorrow.","prescribedDayPatches":[{"date":"2026-10-18","dayType":"long","run":{"type":"long","distanceM":25750,"structure":"12 mi steady easy, then 4 mi at MP 8:00 – 8:05/mi. Gel at 45 and 90 min, drink to a schedule.","paceOrHr":"First 12 mi 9:30 – 9:50/mi, HR under 150. Last 4 mi 8:00 – 8:05/mi.","shoes":"Brooks Ghost 16"},"notes":"Open at 9:45/mi, nothing faster than 9:30 before mile 4, then roll into MP. If the Achilles whispers in the first 10 miles, drop the MP and jog home."}],"safetyCallouts":[{"title":"Check in with your physio before Sunday","severity":"caution","body":"The right Achilles that spoke up today is the same tendon that flared in September. A quick message to your sports physio before Sunday's long run is the safe call — a mid-run settle is reassuring, not a green light.\\n\\nWatch three things this week: morning stiffness that lasts past the first mile, pain that sharpens with pace, or anything above 2/10 that climbs during a run. If any of those show up, the MP finish comes off Sunday and tell me."}],"settingsProposalBullets":["Shoe preference update: use Saucony Endorphin Speed 4 for long runs and marathon-pace work for the rest of this block; Brooks Ghost 16 stays for daily easy miles. Hold the switch until the Achilles is clearly quiet (earliest the long run of Oct 25 – 26)."]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24761,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6631,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard","output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5425}},"diagnostics":null}	200	88771	tool_use	24761	6631	0	0	ok	\N	5425
