d0354e8d-f8df-491d-ba24-f08a0e89f48f	coach	The Achilles signal from Thursday is the whole story this week — we pull quality out, keep running only if pain stays low and not worsening, and you get it looked at by a sports physio.	2026-09-13 20:00:00+00	48424895-cef1-450a-ab68-121423204d3a	\N	97c8e581-f250-477f-a7db-2269194dbe8b	7	\N	[{"body": "Pain that sharpens with pace and lingers as morning stiffness is worth a professional look, not a wait-and-see. Please book a sports physio or sports medicine doctor in the next few days — they can tell you what's going on and what loading is safe.\\n\\nStop running and seek same-day care if you get sudden sharp pain, a pop or snap sensation, visible swelling, or you can't push off the foot normally. I'm coaching the training around this; the medical read needs to come from a qualified professional.", "title": "Get the Achilles assessed this week", "severity": "caution"}]	weekly_read	\N
